1 NOTE Name: Hannah ATHERALD Sex: F Change Date: 03 MAR 2004 Reference Number: GAV9 Note:
2 CONT info from Jess Ball  Grandmother of Mary Ball and Grt Grandmother of President GeorgeWashington. Also Ancestor of President James Madison
2 CONT Burial: Millenbeck,Lancaster,Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ball was living in 1691, as the Assembly of Virginia, held at James City 16 April 1691, passed an act establishing a port in Lancaster county, 'on the land wehre Mrs. Hannah Ball now liveth scituate on the Westerne side of th
2 CONC e mouth of Cototoman River. (Ref: Hennings Revised Statutes, Vol. III, p. 60). She is also referenced in her son William's will of 1694.
2 CONT  per WFT 12-2357: "Hannah made out a will fifteen years after her husband 's death leavinga negro slave to her daughter Hannah, who had been rebuked in Colonel Wi lliam Ball's will." per WFT E1-0515: "Hannah's parentage is mention
2 CONC ed in Earl Heck's Colone l William Ball of VA, The Great Grandfather of Washington, London, 1928 . This book refers unspecifically to Hayden. 1
2 CONT Birth: 1616 in Burgh, Suffolk, England 2 Death: 25 JUN 1695 in Millenbeck, Lancaster Co., VA 2 3 Burial: Millenbeck, Lancaster Co., VA Note: GAV-9
2 CONT Will of Hannah Ball:  In the name of God, Amen, I, Hannah Ball, widow and relict of Coll. William Ball late of the County of Lancaster, do make and ordain this to be my last will and testament.  Item. I give and bequeath to my lov
2 CONC ing daughter Hannah, one negro or Mulatto girl named, being increase of a negro woman named Bess given unto me by husband, Coll. William Ball.  Item. I give and bequeath unto my grandson William Ball one negro woman named Bess.  I
2 CONC tem. My grandson James Ball.  Item. My daughter Hannah Fox and Grandson William Ball executors.  I set my seal in the year of our Lord 1695 June 25.
2 CONT  Hannah Atherold died 1695 at Millenbck, Laancaster Co., Va. See page 32, Colonel William Ball of Virginia, by- Earl L. W. Heck. Hannah Atherold was daughter of Thomas Atherold, son of Thomas Atherold of Burgh, Suffolk and was bor
2 CONC n about 1590. His mother was Mary Vessey. Hannah Atherold's mother was Mary Harvey, a daughter of John Harvey of London.
2 CONT 1
2 CONT  Father: Thomas ATHEROLD  b: 16 AUG 1590 in Burgh, Suffolk, England  Mother: Mary (Hannah) HARVEY b: 1595 in London, England  Marriage 1 William BALL b: ABT 1615 in Wiltshire (London?), England
2 CONT Married: 02 JUL 1638 in London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Cowart Family database compiled by Richard Cowart (rickc@anv.net) gives following: Ball, Mrs. Hannah, wido Col. Wm. Ball. 25 Jun 1695. Rec. 120ct. 1695. Daus. Mrs. Hannah Fox; Gr. sons, William Ball and James Ball. Extrs. dau. Han
2 CONC nah Fox, and gr. son William Ball. Wits. Richard Sanderson and Hannah Ball. W.B. 8, p.51. Will Book 8, p.102. June 25, 1695 Lancaster Co., Virginia: In the name of God, Amen, I, Hannah Ball, wido and relict of Col. William Ball la
2 CONC te of the County of Lancaster, do make and ordain this to be last will and testament. I give and bequeath to my loving daughter Hannah, one negro or Mulatto girl named........, being increase of a negor woman named Bess given unto
2 CONC  me by husband, Col. William Ball. I give and bequeath unto my grandson William Ball one negro woman named Bess. My grandson James Ball. 5. My daughter Hannah fox and Grandson William Ball executors. I set my seal in the year of o
2 CONC ur Lord 1695-June 25. Cowart postulates that Col. William originally came to the colonies in 1635 on the ship Planter with his father and five brothers. He must have returned to England where he & Hannah were married in London in 
2 CONC 1638. Their first son, Richard, was born in Virginia & died in infancy. They returned to England, where their remaining three children were born, coming back to Virginia about 1650. He was probably completing his law education, an
2 CONC d operated a ship while living with his brother before purchasing his plantation in 1657.
