1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Capt. William Ball, II of Millenbeck''' was born on June 2, 1641 in England, UK. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-32875410293 Col. William Ball of &quot;Millenbeck&quot;] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-33544579
2 CONC  Hannah (Atherold) Ball]. He was a Sir William of Millenbeck,Captain,Colonel States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-10079856 Margaret (Williamson) Ball] before November 10, 1672 in Virginia, Colonial America. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-23126079 Margaret D
2 CONC ownman Chinn]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-23126077 Richard Ball, of Lancaster, VA]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-23126078 Sir James of Bewdley Major James Ball]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-10079917 Sir Joseph of Coan Captai
2 CONC n Ball]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-23126082 David Ball]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-23124391 Samuel Ball]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-23126083 Stretchley Ball]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-21784319 Col. William Ball, o
2 CONC f &quot;Millenbeck&quot;]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34646871150 Capt. George Ball, of Bayview]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717461712 Ann (Ball) Moreland]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on September 30, 1694 in Millenbeck, Lancaster County, Virginia, Colonial America and was buried in October 1694 in St. Mary&#39;s White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia, Colonial America. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT In his fathers will William inherited the home plantation known as Millenbeck. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The long accepted statement that Capt. Ball married three times is incorrect, as substantiated by his will, 29 Dec 1694, when wife Margaret was still living, the information in a 1709 deed listing all 8 of his children by Margaret
2 CONC  Williamson Ball -- Richmond County VA Deed Bk 5, pp 211-216 
2 CONT
2 CONT  In 1670, William is referenced as a member of the House of Burgess and by 1680, it is reported that he was serving as a Justice. In 1687 he was appointed to lay off the boundry's between, Lancaster & Northumberland Co's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children include
2 CONT # George.  Married Judith Payne
2 CONT # Sarah Ball b. 1700-5.  Married 1) Dennis McCarty 2) Abram Barnes
2 CONT # Judith. Married 1) George Glasscock 13 Apr 13 1726
2 CONT # Ellen.  Married 1) Richard Chichester 2) Wm. Downman 12 June 1747
2 CONT
