1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parents: William Ball b: 2 JUN 1611 in London, England and Hannah Atherold b: 2 FEB 1617/18 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ball family line connects to George Washington through his maternal lineage. Joseph Ball was the father to George Washington's Mother, Mary Ball Washington. DNA studies do not bear out this relationship with President George W
2 CONC ashington (see comments on Col. William Ball's profile).
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Ball (1649-1711) was born in England and came to Virginia sometime before his father's death, making his home at a plantation called Epping Forest. (This was also the estate where Mary Ball Washington, mother of the first P
2 CONC resident of the United States, was born). Joseph served as a justice of the county court, a vestryman for his church parish, as a Member of the House of Burgess (in 1698, 1700, and 1702), and as a lieutenant colonel in the county 
2 CONC militia. Possible middle name: Matthaus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Joseph Ball's will was proven 15 Nov 1721. Abstracts of Lancaster County, Virginia Wills 1653-1800; {Ida J. Lee} BALL, Joseph,. Psh. St. Mary's White Chapel. Will. 25 June 1711. Rec. 11 July 1711. Wife Mary; son Joseph; da
2 CONC us. Hannah Travers; Anne Conway; Esther Chinn; Elizabeth Cornegie; Mary Ball; Eliza Johnson (dau. of his wife), dau. Mary, 400 acres of land in Richmond county; grandson James Cornegie (not 21) acknowledges gift to son Joseph Ball
2 CONC , and daus. Hannah Travers, Anne Conway and Esther Chinn made 11 Feb. 1707; Overseer John Hagan; negroes formerly belonging to Jon. Carnegie, decd. Extr. Joseph Ball. Wits. Geo. Finch, Elizabeth Finch, Margaret Miller, Joseph Tayl
2 CONC or. W.B. 10, p. 88.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Joseph Ball signed a will on 25 Jun 1711 in Lancaster Co., VA. in which he named step daughter, Elizabeth Johnson, 100 A. of land for life this is used for proof of marriage in this source. He had an estate probated on 11 Jul
2 CONC  1711 in Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1-Female MNU Ball b: ABT 1653 in London, England Married: ABT 1669 in London, England.  '''This marriage and child are not firmly proven.''' Children: John Ball b: 1670 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT From his marriage to Elizabeth Romney, who died by the early 1700's, he had five children listed in his will of 1711.  The oldest child, daughter Frances, died in 1699.  This wife's name has been seen as Julia or Elizabeth Julia  
2 CONC but I have seen no documentation for it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 2-Elizabeth Romney b: ABT 1659 in London, England Married: 1675 in London, England. From his marriage to Elizabeth Romney, who died by the early 1700's, he had five children listed in his will of 1711. This wife's name ha
2 CONC s been seen as Julia or Elizabeth Julia  but I have seen no documentation for it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Frances Ball b: 1680 in Lancaster County, Virginia, d: 1699.
2 CONT #  Hannah Ball b: 1683 in Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT #  Easter Ball b: 1685 in Millenbeck, Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Ball b: 1685 in Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT #  Anne Ball b: 3 OCT 1686 in Christ Church Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia - Probate
2 CONT #  Joseph Ball b: 11 MAR 1688/89 in Morattico, Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 3-Mary '''Johnson''' (died 1721), a widow who had two children from her previous marriage. Together they had one child, a daughter named Mary Ball (1708-1789). Joseph passed away, however, soon after when Mary Ball was on
2 CONC ly three years old.  Mary Johnson Ball was remarried the following year to a man named Richard Hewes, who left her a widow for the third time in 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage 3 Mary {Unproven} Bennett b: 1665 in West Chester, England Married: 1708 in Lancaster County, Virginia''' '''(conflict in surname of 3rd wife?)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #  Mary Ball b: NOV 1708 in "Epping Forest", Lancaster County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # Roberts, Gary Boyd. Ancestors of American Presidents. (Boston, Massachusetts: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2009), p. 1. Maternal grandfather of George Washington. Joseph Ball, England. 24 May 1649, Epping Forest, L
2 CONC ancaster Co. between 25 June and 11 July 1711, c. 1707-8 (post 6 Feb. 1707) m. Mrs. Mary (___) Johnson. [Note that "Epping Forest" did not exist by that name until 1843. It was simply known as the "The Forest" or "The Forest Quart
2 CONC er." [1
2 CONT # Lancaster Will Book 10, in Lancaster Will Book 10, p. 88-93, 88-93 .
