1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1.	David Ball was a twin brother with Stretchley Ball who died in infancy.  They were born 26 SEP 1686 in Lancaster Co., VA.,  David Ball died 14 DEC 1732 in Lancaster Co., VA.. He was buried AFT 14 DEC 1732 in Lan
2 CONC caster Co., VA. - White Chapel Cemetery. He was the son of 2. William Ball and 3. Margaret Williamson. He married Mary Ann 'Ellen' Heale 29 MAY 1727 in Lancaster Co., VA., daughter of George Nicholas Heale and Catherine Chinn. She
2 CONC  was born 09 NOV 1705 in North Farnham Parish, Richmond, VA..
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT !9--7. David, b. Sept. 26, 1686; d. Dec. 14, 1732; m. (first) Mary-; (second) May 29, 1727, Ellen Heale, dau. of George Heale, of Lancaster Co., Va.;
2 CONT
2 CONT James, David, Stretchley and Samuel Ball received various lands in Richmond County to be equally divided.
2 CONT
2 CONT !13 Dec 1732: Will of David Ball, St. Mary's White Chapel, Recorded 14 March 1732. Nephews: David son of Geo Ball; George, son of Geo. Ball; Joseph son of Geo Ball Sr.; Joseph son of Joseph Ball; Wm Ball son of Wm Ball. Brothers: 
2 CONC Samuel, William and James Ball. extrs. James and George Ball. Wits. George and Jesse Ball. "I give to the church (St. Mary's White Chapel) one large bible, one large common prayer book and one good service book. I desire to be bur
2 CONC ied at the ch. and to have a stone of ten pounds price." W. B. 13, p. 91. Ida J. Lee, Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills 1653-1800, The Dietz Press, Inc., Richmond, VA, 1959.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT Re: his wid. m. (second) Dec. 20, 1736, Moore Fauntleroy. From Colonial Families of the Southern States.  That is incorrect; it was Ann Heale, daughter of John Heale, who married Moore Fauntleroy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
