1 NAME William /Fox/
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Fox
2 _MARNM Fox
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 JAN 1670
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1718
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 3. William Fox, b. 20 Jan 1673/4. 0
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Ann Chinn, daughter of John-1 and Alice Chinn. His 1718 will names wife Ann and only one child, a daughter Mary, who apparently died young. She is not named in the will of her mother, Ann (Chinn) Fox Chichester (widow of R
2 CONC ichard Chichester, her 2nd husband). We believe this is how a fictional daughter Mary that was added to some of the published genealogies as a child of David-2 Fox and Hannah Ball. His will also names "Sister" Catherine Heale, wif
2 CONC e of George Heale. Again, she was a sister-in-law, and she was Catherine Chinn, another daughter of John-1 and Alice Chinn. And again, some have turned her into a blood sister of WIlliam Fox and such is not the case.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/VA-NORTHERN-NECK/2011-09/1315956181
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT (1) "Mostly Southern," by Mark Freeman (http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com, markfreeman database, 6 Jul 2007).
2 CONT (2) "The Chinn and Myers Families," by Randie Myers (http://wc.rootsweb.com, rjm66 database, 29 Apr 2007). Cites: (a) "Colonial Families of the Southern United States of America." (b) "William and Mary College Quarterly Historical
2 CONC  Magazine," Vol. 5, No. 4 (Apr. 1897) p.260-261. (c) Lancaster Co., Wills, etc. No 8 (1690-1709) p.210-211. Copied from a handwritten copy in the Chinn Family file #73 developed by Miss Nanon L. Carr and located in the Mid-Contine
2 CONC nt Genealogy Library, Independence, MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: (1) Abt 1682. (2a) s/o David FOX/Hannah BALL. 20 Jan 1672/3. VA.
2 CONT Marriage to Ann CHINN: (1) 11 Jul 1719. (1,2) Lancaster Co., VA. (2) Aug 1701.
2 CONT Death: (2b) 1718. VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2b) 1701: Burgess, Lancaster Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2c) 1701, 29 Aug: Alice STRETCHLEY of the parish of St Mayries, White Chapell in the Co. of Lancr made her will. "I give unto my Son in Law Capt Wm FOX all the rest residue & remarnder of what money is of mine in the hands of Mr 
2 CONC Tho ELLIS of London Mercht Excepting and Reserved to the use of Edward AUDLEY (was Jno STRETCHLEY's nephew) one hundred pounds Sterling left him by my husband Mr Jno STRETCHLEY which I will that my sd Son Wm FOX see him paid of th
2 CONC e sd money in ELLIS his? hands and in case of his death then the sd hundred pounds I give to my sd son Wm FOX as also all the rest of the money in his the sd ELLIS his hands Except what is bereby before bequeathed in full Leiu of 
2 CONC and in full Satisfaction of any futher claims or Chalange to any other part or parcell of my sd estate."
2 CONT
2 CONT *Reference: [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=adgedge&id=I48469 RootsWeb's WorldConnect] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 1 2016, 7:49:43 UTC''
