1 NAME Sarah /Ball/
2 GIVN Sarah
2 SURN Ball
2 _MARNM Selden
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1701
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 6 AUG 1742
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Ball, daughter of Richard Ball and Sarah Young, married John Selden, son of Samuel Selden; his 2nd wife, on 13 Oct 1725 in Lancaster County, Virginia.  She died before about 1740, when he married Grace Boswel
2 CONC l.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Ball was the mother of Richard Selden, mentioned in her mother's will.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Abstract of Sarah Ball, in Lee, Ida J. Abstracts Lancaster County, Virginia, Wills, 1653-1800. (Richmond: Dietz Press, 1959). p 7-8 - 
2 CONT
2 CONT BALL, Sarah. Will. 6 Aug. 1742. Rec. 10 Sept. 1742. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Legatees: Daus. Easter Glascock, [Mrs.] Margaret Ball, [Mrs.] John Selden, Gr. son Wm. Montague, Gr. Dau. Frances Lawry. Extr. Wm. Glasscock. Mention is made of a marriage betw. her gr. son Richard Seldon and the dau. of James Bal
2 CONC l. Wits. Margaret Williamson, Eliz. McTire and Wm. Ball. W.B. 13, p. 301.
2 CONT
2 CONT BALL, Sarah. Inventory & Appraisement. Rec. 9 Otober [sic] 1742. Returned by Wm. Glasscock, Extr. W.B. 13, p. 290. Division of Negroes held by Sarah Ball as dower of estate of her husband Richard Ball, decd. recorded 12 Nov. 1742.
2 CONC  Divided between Mrs. Margaret Ball, Mr. Wm. Glasscock, Mr. Richard Selden and Mr. William Montague. W.B. 13, p. 294.
2 CONT
2 CONT BALL, Sarah, widow. Inventory, rec. 9 March 1743. Returned by Wm. Glasscock, Gent. Extr. W.B. 14, p. 10  [Identified as daughter of Mrs. Sarah Ball, wife of John Seldon and mother of Richard Seldon.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
