1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Genealogies of Virginia Families", pg. 474:
2 CONT
2 CONT :Thomas Dameron, and Winifred were witnesses to a will March 20, 1726. Winifred died shortly after this and '''Thomas Dameron married about 1730, his third wife, Ann, widow of John Pope and daughter of Capt. George Ball.''' 
2 CONT :Capt. George Ball, son of Capt. William Ball, was born about 1680. According to family history, he was married twice. The surname of his first wife is unknown. By this first marriage there were two or three children, among them A
2 CONC nn, born probably in 1702 or 3. The court records clearly prove that George Ball was married to Grace Haynie, daughter of Anthony and Sarah Harris Haynie before 1709, as Anthony Haynie in his will dated June 31, 1709, mentions his
2 CONC  daughter Grace Ball.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Will of John Pope, made Jan. 4, 1722, as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT * I leave to my wife Ann Pope the use of the manor plantation, lying between my son's Joseph and John Pope's land during her natural life and after her decease, to my son John Pope and his heirs.
2 CONT * My will is that my four sons shall have their estate paid them when they come to the age of eighteen, the residue of my estate unto my dear and loving wife, Ann Pope, and my four sons.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Ann_Ball_%285%29 WeRelate Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 31 2016, 1:32:20 UTC''
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I25681&tree=Tree1
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/70556807/ann-dameron-pope date errors?
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:George_Ball_%2875%29
