2 CONC . Jane Montgomery Simpson Robert Montgomery Goodall ancestors descendants (June 19, 1853 - December 12, 1917) Warner Lewis ancestors (June 24, 1755 - February 1756) George Washington Lewis ancestors (March 13, 1757 - November 13, 
2 CONC 1821) m. Catherine Dangerfield Miriam (Lewis) Madison ancestors descendants (1762 - 1845) m. Gabriel Madison Gabriella Anna (Madison) Hawkins ancestors descendants (1794 - May 11, 1884) m. Strother Hawkins Myra (Hawkins) Banks anc
2 CONC estors descendants (1818 - 1889) m. David Banks Margaret (Banks) Sebree ancestors (1833 - ) Ethelinda Esther (Hawkins) Hopkins ancestors descendants (May 1, 1820 - February 8, 1873) m. John Hopkins Annah G. Hopkins ancestors (1849
2 CONC  - 1857) John Taylor Hopkins Jr. ancestors descendants (June 6, 1852 - October 31, 1938) m. Lizzie Hickman Hickman Madison Hopkins ancestors descendants (August 4, 1875 - August 1, 1947) John Taylor Hopkins III ancestors (October 
2 CONC 21, 1877 - January 17, 1948) Ethal Linda Hopkins ancestors (September 1879 - ) William Hopkins ancestors (July 1881 - ) Strother Banks Hopkins ancestors (August 20, 1854 - 1926) Strother Hawkins Jr ancestors (1830 - ) Gabriella Ha
2 CONC wkins ancestors (1833 - ) Margaret Hawkins ancestors (1836 - ) Betty (Lewis) Carter ancestors (February 23, 1765 - April 9, 1830) Lawrence Lewis ancestors (March 4, 1767 - November 20, 1839) m. Eleanor Custis Robert Lewis ancestor
2 CONC s (June 25, 1769 - January 17, 1829) Howell Lewis ancestors (December 12, 1771 - December 26, 1822) m. Ellen Hackley Pollard
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Betty Washington was the only sister of President George Washington that lived to adulthood. Betty married Fielding Lewis and together they lived in Fredericksburg, Virginia. Fielding built the Kenmore estate in Fredericksburg whi
2 CONC ch became their new home. After her husband's death in 1781 Betty moved to Western View plantation in Culpeper, Virginia to live with her daughter. Betty Washington spent the remaining days of her life there until her death in 179
2 CONC 7. (bio by: Marvin Sport) 
2 CONT
