1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 131
2 CONT Samuel Washington was born at Wakefield, on Pope's Creek, Westmoreland Co., VA., the birthplace of his brother George and his sister Elizabeth (Betty) on November 27 (N.S.), 1734, "about 3 in ye Morning."
2 CONT He lived as a boy in 3 different counties of Virginia, Westmoreland, Prince William and Stafford; as a man he lived and held public office in three, Stafford, Frederick and Berkeley, but he never was an old man; he died at the age
2 CONC  of 47.  Harewood was his home for 11 years, 1770 to 1781.
2 CONT JOHN ALEXANDER, A NORTHERN NECK PROPRIETOR, HIS FAMILY, FRIENDS & KIN by Wesley Pippenger
2 CONT Col. Samuel Washington was born 16 Nov. 1734 at Wakefield in Stafford Co.  He went to Jefferson Co., W.V. where he died 1781.  His estate "Harewood".  He was the son of Augustine Washington.
2 CONT Note:  There is some differences in the above but found that Samuel Washington was in the county of Stafford at that time. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - Ibid, p. 143
2 CONT Jane Champe, daughter of Col. John Champe of King George Co.,VA.  If she had any children they died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - Ibid
2 CONT Mildred Thornton, daughter of Col. John Thornton and his wife Mildred Gregory.  Mildred had two sons: Thornton, born probably in 1760 who grew up and married; and Tristram, born in or about 1763, who did not grow up.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #3 - Ibid
2 CONT Lucy Chapman, daughter of Nathaniel Chapman died in 1762 of childbirth.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #4 - Ibid
2 CONT Anne Steptoe, daughter of Col. William Steptoe. She is said to have been the widow of Willoughby Allerton when she married Samuel Washington, probably in the autumn of 1766.  She had at least 4 Washington children:: Ferdinand, bor
2 CONC n July 16, 1767; George Steptoe, Lawrence Augustine and Harriet, who married Parks.  All of Anne's children must have been born prior to December 1780, since Samuel Washington married his fifth wife not later than that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #5 - Ibid
2 CONT The Widow Holding, who seems to have been born Susannah Perrin.  She had a son, John Perrin Washington, who was born prior to Sept. 9, 1781 when Samuel Washington made his will.  
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died in 1781.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - See below
2 CONT He is buried in the grave yard south of the house.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a metal tablet bearing the following inscription:
2 CONT HAREWOOD
2 CONT ERECTED IN 1771.  THE HOME OF COL.
2 CONT SAMUEL WASHINGTON, COUNTY LIEUTENANT
2 CONT HIS BROTHER GENERAL GEORGE WASHINGTON
2 CONT VISITED HERE AND GENERAL LAFAYETTE
2 CONT AND LOUIS PHILLIPE OF FRANCE WERE
2 CONT ENTERTAINED HERE.  IN THIS HOUSE 
2 CONT JAMES MADISON AND DOLLY PAYNE TODD
2 CONT WERE MARRIED.  SAMUEL WASHINGTON
2 CONT DIED IN 1781 AND IS BURIED IN THE
2 CONT GRAVE YARD SOUTH OF THE HOUSE
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT George Steptoe Washington (1770-1809) lived at Harewood, the home of his father, Col. Samuel Washington.  His wife was Lucy Payne, a sister to Dolly Payne Todd; and thus it came about that the marriage of James Madison and Dolly P
2 CONC ayne Todd, in September 1794 took place at Harewood.  The officiating clergyman was Rev. Alexander Balmain, a chaplain of the Revolution and for many years thereafter a well-known minister of Winchester and the surrounding region.
2 CONC  - Ibid
