1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT "...'''John Augustine Washington''' (1736–1787) was a member of the fifth Virginia Convention and a founding member of the Mississippi Land Company. During the American Revolution he was a member of Westmoreland County's Committee
2 CONC  of Safety and the Chairman of the County Committee for Relief of Boston..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...He was the brother of President George Washington and the third son of Mary Ball and Augustine Washington. John Washington married Hannah Bushrod in 1756, and lived with her in the family estate, Mount Vernon. One of their chi
2 CONC ldren was Supreme Court Justice Bushrod Washington..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': Wikipedia contributors, 'John Augustine Washington', ''Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia'', 23 November 2010, 22:15 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=John_Augustine_Washington&oldid=398520664> [accessed 4
2 CONC  September 2011]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Find A Grave Memorial # 103950416:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Augustine Washington was a Colonel in the Virginia Militia, a member of the Virginia Conventions of 1775-76, married @ Westmoreland County, ca. 14 April 1756, to Hannah Bushrod eldest daughter and co-heiress of Col. John Bush
2 CONC rod, of Bushfield, JP and Burgess, and only daughter by his 1st wife Jane Corbin (the daughter of Hon. Gawin Corbin, Pres of Gov's Council). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/person-1505022_429422831_429422831/john-augustine-washington MyHeritage Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 25 2018, 19:42:06 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Enslaved and possible son of:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.mountvernon.org/george-washington/slavery/paternity-of-west-ford/
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.geni.com/people/West-Ford/6000000199688702836
