1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Also seen as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Ball/6000000003858746097?through=6000000197822754821 & https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Ball/6000000003858656623?through=6000000197822754821
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT sarah martha ball's lineage is uncertain. discussion below and, most recently, here: http://www.geni.com/discussions/122705
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Martha Ball, born 30 Dec 1712 in Plymouth Township, Pennsylvania; died 10 Dec 1779 in Montgomery County, Pennsylvania. She was the daughter of '''John Ball''' and '''Sarah Roades'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Birth date given as tenth month which in Quaker records for 1712 would mean December. Source of information Tom Taylor in answer from Susanna Morikawa, Archival Specialist at Swarthmore's Friends Library, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Abt. 1737 in Pennsylvania to Paul Custer (1710-1783), son of Arnold Custer & Rebecca.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # Jonathan Custer, Sr., born 04 Oct 1738 in Montgomery County, Pennsylvania; died Bef. 13 Nov 1823 in Amityville, Berks County, Pennsylvania; married Hannah Peters Abt. 1759 in Pennsylvania.
2 CONT # George Custer, Sr., born Dec 1744 in Pennsylvania; died 17 Dec 1829 in Georges Township, Fayette County, Pennsylvania married (1) Susannah Long Mar 1774; born 13 May 1755; died 17 Oct 1784 in Hagerstown, Frederick County, MD; ma
2 CONC rried (2) Catherine Leatherman 28 Nov 1784; born 07 Apr 1765 in Frederick County, Maryland; died 22 Sep 1844 in Georges Township, Fayette County, Pennsylvania (Source: Headstone in Collier Cemetery.).
2 CONT # Nicholas Custer, born Abt. 1745; died Unknown.
2 CONT # William Custer, born Abt. 1740; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH: Her birth was recorded at the Gwynned Monthly Meeting of Friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sarah's nephew was Joseph Ball, a very wealthy man who died intestate and without issue 28 Apr 1821 in Philadelphia. There have been many attempts to tie this Ball family to George Washington's mother but, as of yet, no success. 
2 CONC )Source: The Descendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters)
2 CONT
2 CONT * from the postem http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gdecourcy&id=I003542
2 CONT
2 CONT >Samuel Ball and his wife, Sarah Tayloe did not have a daughter named Sarah ... Samuel died when his children were underage ... and under guardian bond - Samuel died 1752 - and there were only five children... 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Judith Ball b: 1718 m: John Hackley  
2 CONT # Margaret Ball b: 1724 m: John Barrow  
2 CONT # Mary Ball b: 1732 m: Robert Green  
2 CONT # William Ball b: 1734 m: Frances Slaughter  
2 CONT # Susanna Ball b: Nov 1737 m: John Lillard 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is apparent the continued confusion concerning the Pennsylvania Ball familial relationships were forever damaged by the famous ... Ball Estate Association ... fabricated confabulation contines to work its damage a hundred years
2 CONC  after the fact. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Someone should go to the Library of Congress ... remove that publlcation and ........... BURN IT...! 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~mcclell2/homepage/richball.htm
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/e/b/n/Grace--Ebneter/GENE1-0019.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # Margaret B. Kinsey in "Ball Cousins" compiled a book based on the distribution of Joseph Ball's estate between 1827 and 1858 which is a great help to researchers in sorting out the family of Sarah Ball Custer and also shows no r
2 CONC elationship to the Washington family.  Margaret Kinsey, Ball Cousins, (Gateway Press, Baltimore, Maryland 1981)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=X8EwAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA65&ots=D0gtHQiCqw&dq=Ball%20Estate%20Association&pg=PA65#v=onepage&q=Ball%20Estate%20Association&f=false A Pennsylvania Pioneer: ] Biographical Sketch with Report of the Execu
2 CONC tive ... By Emmett William Gans
2 CONT
2 CONT
