2 CONT 5. Lucy Chilton 1775 – 1855<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Interesting Notes<br/>
2 CONT There is a book named "They Behaved Like Soldiers: Captain John Chilton and the Third Virginia Regiment 1775-1778"
2 CONT
2 CONT President George Washington and John Chilton were 2nd cousins. John's grandmother Lettice "Letitia" Mary Ball was 1st cousins with George's mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Updated Oct 4, 2015
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died on battlefield at Brandywine Delaware Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried at Rock Spring, Prince William County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT from genealogy.com In a recent visit to the Yorktown, VA museum I found the following:YORKTOWN, VA. MUSEUM:The CHILTON coat of arms and the following citation:
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN CHILTON, 1739-1777 "A Southern Planter Longs for Home. John Chilton was a planter from Fauquier County, Virginia. In 1775, he supported the American cause by organizing a company of volunteers for a local militia unit.After t
2 CONC he sudden death of his wife, Letitia, Chilton placed his five young children in the care of a brother.He then joined theContinental army as a captain in the 3rd Virginia Regiment.A steadfast supporter of American independence, Chi
2 CONC ltonwas wounded and died on the field during the Battle of Brandywine, near Philadelphia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chilton's wartime thoughts survive in letters and a small diary that vividly portray life in the Continental army.He asked his family about the welfare of his children, and described his fellow officers, the war, and what he ate."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Captain John Chilton and wife Letitia (Blackwell) Chilton are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Chiltonb. 10 May 1769 d. 1843 m.Jane Corbin
2 CONT
2 CONT George Chiltonb. 5 July 1770 d. 4 Nov 1852 m.Mary Ellen Ball
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Chiltonb. 8 Oct 1771 d. 1820 m.Agustine Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Chiltonb.20 Dec 1773 d.26 Oct 1855 m.Lt. John Ransdell28 Nov 1792 It appears Lucy and John Ransdell had 13 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Chiltonb. 1774 d. 4 Sept 1841 m. Ann Smith
