1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lancaster Marriage Bonds 1717-1739 at http://www.rootsweb.com/~valancas/marriagebonds.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 June, 1757, Col. John Payne & Jean Chichester. Sec. George Heale. This was Jean Smith who married (JUL 1752) John Chichester (1735-1753/4)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT CHICHESTER, John. Will. 14 Sept. 1753. Rec. 15 March 1754. Wife Jean, plantation I now live on. Dau. Mary Chichester; brother Richard Chichester, four sisters, Elizabeth, Ellen, Mary and Hannah. Brother Rawleigh Downman; Miss Eliz
2 CONC abeth Griffin. Extrs. James Ball, Jr., Richd. Chichester. No witnesses. W.B. 15, Page 168.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT CHICHESTER, Richard. Will. 16 May 1743. Rec. 10 Aug. 1744. Wife Ellen; Sons: Richard and John; Daughters: Elizabeth, Ellen, Mary and Hannah. Mentions estate in England. Extrs. Wife Ellen, son John; friends: Jesse Ball, Robt. Mitch
2 CONC ell and Jos. Carter, Amy Carter, Gawin Lowry, Michael Dillon. W.B. 14, Page 29.
2 CONT Record 10 Mch. 1748 of settlement of estate. Mr. Wm. Downman's part in right of his wife Ellen, widow of sd. Richard. W.B. 14, Page 232.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT
