1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susannah Oldham was born 1 JAN 1746 in Prince William County, Colonial Virginia, and died 1819 in Louisville, Jefferson County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT She was the daughter of John Oldham and Ann Conway
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT # Lawrence Ross, Patriot Soldier 1762 in Northampton or Hampshire County, Colonial Virginia, son of William Ross and Arminella WHITESIDE. He was born 15 MAY 1722 in the Goose Creek area, Prince William County, Colonial Virginia ne
2 CONC ar Rectortown, and died 18 AUG 1818 in Jefferson County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT #  Shapley Prince Ross, Sr. b: 12 FEB 1763 in Hampshire County, Colonial Virginia
2 CONT #  Elizabeth 'Betsy' Ross b: 1769
2 CONT #  Mary 'Polly' Ross b: 21 NOV 1769 in Loudoun County, Colonial Virginia
2 CONT #  Nancy Ross b: 29 NOV 1771 in Botetourt County, Colonial Virginia (now Jefferson County, Kentucky)
2 CONT #  Susannah Ross b: 13 SEP 1773
2 CONT #  Mildred 'Milly' Ross b: 1784
2 CONT #  Ann Ross b: 1785
2 CONT #  Frances R. 'Fanny' Ross b: 7 APR 1786
2 CONT #  Sarah 'Sally' Ross
2 CONT #  Presley Nevil Ross b: 1790 in Jefferson County, Kentucky
2 CONT #  William Ross
2 CONT #  Lawrence Ross, II
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT "Susannah's [GRAND] mother was a half-sister to Mary Ball Washington, mother of George Washington. Ann Ball/Oldham married second to Darby Aughney. Dorthy Ross of Rochester, Illinois, provided this sketch."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Nancy L. Carter
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Sep 1768: Fairfax Lease to Darby Aughtney, Anne Aughtney and William Oldham rec. 15 Sep 1768 for 400 acres on South Branch, Witnessed by Pet. Hog, Alex White, Gabriel Jones !1795: Samuel Bray was to inherit half the land in Ham
2 CONC pshire Co, VA (now in WV) left to his grandmother, Ann (Conway) Oldham AUGHNEY [1718-1796], by her husband, Darby Aughney [ca. 1714-1795], at the time of Ann's death. Source: 1795 will of Darby Aughney. Ann died April, 1796. Conwa
2 CONC y Rector [1760-1832] was to receive the other half of the land at the same time. He was the son of Nancy Ann Oldham [1744-1818] and Daniel Rector, Sr.[1738-1814]. !Will of Darby Aughney, Hampshire Co. WV, Vol 1, p. 48. He gives to
2 CONC  daughter Wineford Nevil. Sage and Jones, Early Records of Hampshire County, VA, p. 107
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
