1 NOTE !DEATH - VA. GENEALOGIES by Hayden p. 262
2 CONT Walker Conway of "Levelfield", Lancaster, Co., VA drowned about 1786 in the
2 CONT Potomac River near Dipple Parish.  Mr. Conway was a minor when his father died. His mother was his guardian  1757, and Travers Downman, Dec. 1767.  He lived until 1786 on land in Northumberland Co. which he inherited from his
2 CONT grandfather, Samuel Heath.  This land he sold May 9, 1786 to John Hull and
2 CONT Joseph Conway, and resided at his Lancaster estate of "Levelfield".  On the
2 CONT watch of Mr. Conway, found on his person when drowned, the Conway "Arms" were
2 CONT engraved.  This watch, Mr. Eustace, guardian for his children, sold, it being
2 CONT "out of order".
