1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 55
2 CONT Fielding Lewis, Jr. was born Feb. 14, 1751, prob. in Fredericksburg, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #1 - THE BEVERLEY FAMILY OF VIRGINIA compiled by John McGill, p. 831
2 CONT He married a Miss Alexander and settled in Clarke Co., VA. on land willed him by his father, just north of "Old Chapel".
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR #2 - JOHN ALEXANDER A NORTHERN NECK PROPRIETOR HIS FAMILY, FRIENDS AND KIN by Wesley E. Pippenger, p. 272
2 CONT Fielding Lewis, Jr. married in March 1789 to Elizabeth Dade who died after 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fielding, the eldest was remembered rather liberally by his grandmother, Mary Washington, in her will.  To him, then 37, she left her negro man Frederick; also 8 silver tablespoons, half her cooking ware, her blue and white tea ch
2 CONC ina, a bookcase, an oval table, one bed and bedstead, a pair of sheets, a pair of blankets, a white cotton counterpane, 2 tablecloths, 6 red leather chairs, half of her pewter and half of her iron kitchen furniture. - See Birth Re
2 CONC ference
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - JOHN ALEXANDER A NORTHERN NECK PROPRIETOR HIS FAMILY, FRIENDS AND KIN by Wesley E. Pippenger, p. 271-272
2 CONT He died 21 July 1803, prob. in Clarke Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis reportedly settled in Frederick Co. (now Clarke Co.) on part of a 1,000 acre tract willed him by his father in the latter's will of St. George's Parish in Spotsylvania Co. dated 19 Oct 1781, just north of "Old Chapel". - Ibi
2 CONC d
