1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 55
2 CONT Robert Lewis was born June 25, 1769, prob. in Fredericksburg, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died on February 10, 1829 in Fredericsburg, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, one of the younger sons of Col. Fielding Lewis and his wife Betty Washington, was the private secretary of General Washington during a part of the time he was President.  In 1791 he located in Fredericksburg where, as a pr
2 CONC ivate citizen, as mayor of the town, and as a member of the Episcopal Church, he was generally esteemed and beloved.  He was elected mayor in 1820 and served until his death, Feb. 10, 1829.  In 1824, as mayor, he delivered the add
2 CONC ress of welcome to Lafayette. - Ibid
