1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 55
2 CONT Howell Lewis, the son of Fielding Lewis and his wife Betty (Washington) Lewis, was born Dec. 12, 1771.  He was the youngest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - THE DESCENDANTS OF CAPT. THOMAS CARTER by Joseph Lyon Miller, p. 342
2 CONT Howell Lewis married Ellen Hackley Pollard who was a grand niece of General Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - See Birth Reference
2 CONT Later (in 1812) Howell Lewis moved to Kanawha Co., now in West Virginia, where he inherited 1300 acres of land and where he lived until his death in 1822, leaving descendants.  Howell Lewis owned 1000 acres in now Clarke Co.,VA, t
2 CONC he place called "Llewellyn," which passed to his brother Lawrence, who sold it to Warner Washington, Jr.
