1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_Augustine_Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT Lawrence Augustine Washington (April 11, 1774 - February 15, 1824) was a nephew of United States President George Washington and son of Samuel Washington and his fourth wife, Anne Steptoe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lawrence was born at Harewood in what is now Jefferson County, West Virginia in 1774. He married Mary Dorcas Wood on November 6, 1797 in Winchester, Virginia. Together, the couple had four children. It is through his son, Dr. Lawr
2 CONC ence Augustine Washington, that a direct Washington family lineage exists today.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. George Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Emma Tell Washington (1812-1838)
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Lawrence Augustine Washington (1813-1882)
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Mary Dorcas Washington (1817-1861)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/105017727/lawrence-augustine-washington Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 29 2019, 1:47:08 UTC''
1 FAMC @F4026036952920010510@
1 FAMS @F4026035703880010554@
1 RFN geni:328066467320004666
1 SUBM @S285725352490006131@
1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 334
2 CONT Lawrence Augustine, born 1768?, son of Col. Samuel Washington and his 4th wife Anne Steptoe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Education directed by General Washington, his uncle. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Mary Dorcas Wood in Frederick Co.,VA Nov. 6, 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived for some time at Hawthorn, part of the Glen Burnie estate at Winchester; removed in 1811 to the Ohio Valley. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT He died near Wheeling, Feb. 15, 1824, in the 56th year of his age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage & Death Notices from the GENIUS OF LIBERTY 1817-1843, p. 9
2 CONT Died on the 15th ult., Laurance Augustine Washington at his residence in Wheeling, age 50 years.
