1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 318
2 CONT Corbin Washington was born 1765, prob. in Westmoreland Co.,VA, the son of John Augustine Washington I and wife Hannah Bushrod.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Hannah Lee, daughter of Richard Henry Lee.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Corbin and his wife, Hannah Lee, lived for many years at Walnut Farm but they died in Fairfax Co. where they were living on October 19, 1799, when Corbin made his will, and in November 1799 when they were visited by General Washin
2 CONC gton.  Corbin and his wife both died soon thereafter.
2 CONT
2 CONT GENEALOGICAL ABSTRACTS FROM 18TH CENTURY VIRGINIA NEWSPAPERS by Robert K. Headley, p. 356
2 CONT WASHINGTON, Corbin, Esq. of Fairfax Co., only surviving brother of Judge Washington and a nephew of of the late Gen. George WASHINGTON, died on the 10th instant at Bushfield, Westmoreland Co. (THE TIMES & DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA DAIL
2 CONC Y ADVERTISER 20 Dec. 1799)
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT They were both buried at "Bushfield" in Westmoreland Co.,VA.
