1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Margaret Burgess, daughter of Charles Burgess and Frances Fox, was born about 1721, and died before 1742. She married James Ball (1718-1789), son of James Ball and Mary Conway, on 1738.  He was the brother of her stepfather Jesse 
2 CONC Ball.  No known children.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I40309&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Charles Burgess and Frances Fox:
2 CONT * 1. Frances Burgess,   b. Abt 1718, St Mary's White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia d. 1750, Lancaster County, Virginia.  Married Baldwin Matthews Smith.
2 CONT *  	2. Margaret Burgess,   b. Abt 1721, St Mary's White Chapel Parish, Lancaster County, Virginia.  Married James Ball (1718 - 1789), son of James Ball and Mary Conway.
2 CONT *  	3. Elizabeth Burgess,   b. 1732, St. Mary's White Chapel, Lancaster County, Virginia d. Between 1754 and 1758, St. Mary's White Chapel, Lancaster County, Virginia. Married 1) Jeduthan Ball (1725-1749), son of  James Ball & Mar
2 CONC y Conway 2) Robert Armistead.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #  https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I40310&tree=Tree1
2 CONT In Christ Church Vestry Book I find that "May 5, 1741, Mr. Jesse Ball and Mrs. Margaret Ball, wife of Mr. James Ball, Jun'r, Mrs. Frances Burgess and Mrs. Elizabeth Burgess, daughters of Charles Burgess, Gent., dec'd, by his wife 
2 CONC Frances, daughter of Samuel Fox, Gent, dec'd, have liberty to build Galleries on the East side of the South wing of the new Church."
