1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LW6K-CWT<br/>
2 CONT '''FamilySearch.org You will need a Free Account to View'''
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT George was the son of Capt. John Chilton who died in the Revolutionary War at the Battle of Brandywine. George Chilton married Mary Ellen Ball January 24, 1792 in Fauquier County, Virginia.<br/>
2 CONT - Contributed by Genie Angel
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT After the Revolutionary War (1776) large numbers of veterans came to Kentucky to claim land grants given to them by Virginia. These and other migrants came into Henry County, Kentucky, via the Wilderness Trail and by river down th
2 CONC e Ohio and up the Kentucky. In 1789 George voted for George Washington. George moved to Henry county in the fall of 1810. <br/>
2 CONT - Contributed by member #48372574
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT The great bulk of early bounty land at the time of the Revolution was in Virginia, as it existed in colonial times. Since Virginia provided the great bulk of fighting men in the Revolution, the first bounty lands were to be locate
2 CONC d between the Mississippi, Ohio and Green Rivers in what is now Kentucky
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT Children of George include:<br/>
2 CONT 1. John Ball Chilton 1792 – 1871<br/>
2 CONT 2. Leticia Blackwell Chilton 1794 – <br/>
2 CONT 3. Charles T Chilton 1798 – <br/>
2 CONT 4. James S Chilton 1799 – 1878<br/>
2 CONT 5. Jane S Chilton 1802 – 1876<br/>
2 CONT 6. George Chilton Jr 1804 – 1859<br/>
2 CONT 7. Mary Chilton 1804 – 1873<br/>
2 CONT 8. Lucy T Chilton 1806 – 1847<br/>
2 CONT 9. Susan Ball Blackwell Chilton 1809 – 1881<br/>
2 CONT - Contributed by Keith Chilton<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/79399043/george-chilton<br/>
