1 OCCU Attorney, Judge, Fayette Co., Representative  & Senator
1 TITL Hon.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Richard Henry Chinn is the son of John Chinn and Mildred Higgins. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chinn is listed as Richard's father on his 16 Apr 1814 marriage license to Elizabeth Holmes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (They are first cousins as Elizabeth's mother is Susannah "Sukey" Chinn, sister of John Chinn - Sukey is the wife of Robert Holmes, Elizabeth's father.)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chinn and Mildred Higgins are said to have 12 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Henry Chinn was a lawyer, said to be the only partner Henry Clay ever had.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also a judge, a Fayette Co. KY Representative and Senator. He continued his legal career in New Orleans where he was an attorney
2 CONT
2 CONT in the famous NOLA Myra Clark Gaines lawsuit . She was the plaintiff in the longest running lawsuit in the U.S. She sued as the sole heir to her father's valuable land. (Daniel Clark - Zulime Carriere , her parents , her husband E
2 CONC dmund Pendleton Gaines )
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Henry and Elizabeth Holmes Chinn's children are :
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Hunter, Cabell Breckenridge, Richard Henry, Melissa Barton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another daughter Eliza Chinn Ripley wrote SOCIAL LIFE IN OLD NEW ORLEANS BEING RECOLLECTIONS OF MY GIRLHOOD.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
