1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT 1653-1800 Lancaster County, Virginia Wills [Ida J. Lee];
2 CONT CHICHESTER, John. Will. 14 Sept. 1753. Rec. 15 March 1754. Wife Jean, plantation I now live on. Dau. Mary Chichester; brother Richard Chichester, four sisters, Elizabeth, Ellen, Mary and Hannah. Brother Rawleigh Downman; Miss Eliz
2 CONC abeth Griffin. Extrs. James Ball, Jr., Richd. Chichester. No witnesses. W.B. 15, Page 168.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I42335&tree=Tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Chichester was born bef 14 Sep 1753 Lancaster County, Virginia. Her parents were John Chichester abt 1735 - bef 1754 and Jean Smith 
2 CONT Marriage to Col. Burgess Ball 2 July 1770 St. James :Northam, Goochland County, Virginia. Col Ball married 2nd Frances Washington Apr 7 1781.
2 CONT Children with Col Burgess Ball:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Burgess Ball
2 CONT Burgess Ball, Jr. b Oct 26 1773
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile was initially created with spouse as Cornelius Leport (abt.1765-) and daughter Melinda Leport Lowell (1798-1877). Both have been removed
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Mary Chichester on werelate
2 CONT ↑ "My Southern Family" (database), online http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~mysouthernfamily, Becky Bonner and Josephine L. Bass, compilers (Oklahoma City, OK), downloaded 26 February 2007.
2 CONT ↑ 3.0 3.1 Col Burgess Ball on rootsweb
