2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE !BIRTH - A GENEALOGY OF THE KNOWN DESCENDANTS OF ROBERT CARTER OF COROTOMAN compiled by Florence Tyler Carlton, p. 324
2 CONT Harriet Bladen Mitchell, daughter of Priscilla Carter and Robet Mitchell, was born 1793.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT She was married to William James Weir and lived at "Liberia" located on part of "Cancer" property of Councillor Robert Carter.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT She died 1841 at "Liberia" her home in Prince William Co., VA.
2 CONT The property is now in the town of Manassas. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - PRINCE WILLIAM, THE STORY OF ITS PLACES AND ITS PEOPLE originally compiled by 1941 by Workers of the Writers Program of the Work Projects Administration in the State of VA., p. 144
2 CONT To the west of the house in the bramble-grown graveyard lies Harriet Bladen Weir (1793-1841).
2 CONT Note:  This grave is not mentioned in PRINCE WILLIAM CO. BURIAL INDEX 1800-1993 by Ronald Ray Turner and it may be that the tombstone is gone or broken as the above book was written in 1961. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT Hariet Bladen Mitchell is 3rd cousin, 3 generations removed to Robert B. Carter.
2 CONT About a quarter of a mile from the highway, among a large group of rather gaunt dairy buildings, 3 m., stands red brick Liberia.  Two-and-a-half-storied and gable-roofed, this plantation house was built about 1825 by William J. We
2 CONC ir (1791-1867).  The estate, however, was originally part of the share of the Lower Bull Run Tract that descended through Councillor Robert Carter to his daughter, Priscilla Mitchell.  Priscilla gave 1,660 acres to her daughter, H
2 CONC arriet Bladen Mitchell, who married William J. Weir.  This child of the proud Carters lived at Mount Grove in Richmond and married an overseer.  But it will be remembered that Councillor Robert joined the Baptist Church and became
2 CONC  a thoroughgoing democrat.  His principles were subjected twice to a severe test - once when his daughter, Ann Tasker, eloped with her tutor and again when he was informed that Priscilla was receiving attentions from an overseer. 
2 CONC   Apparently the Carter-Mitchell alliance caused the Councillor no concern, for he gave to Priscilla the largest slice of his Lower Bull Run Tract - 2,860 acres.  
