1 NOTE !BIRTH - From tombstone
2 CONT Anne Eilbeck McCarty was born in Fairfax Co., VA. 16 July 1785, the only daughter of Col. Daniel McCarty and wife SarahMason.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES by Hayden p. 534
2 CONT John William Bronaugh married Ann Eilbeck, only daughter of Daniel and Sarah
2 CONT Eilbeck (Mason) McCarty.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Tombstone
2 CONT She died in Georgetown, D.C. 6 Feb 1868 in the 83rd year of her age.
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Congressional Cemetery, Washington, D.C., Range 42, Site #149
2 CONT Tombstone (on same tombstone as husband)
2 CONT Anne E. McCarty Bronaugh
2 CONT Daughter of Daniel & Sarah McCarty
2 CONT Born in Fairfax Co.
2 CONT July 16, 1785
2 CONT Died in Georgetown, D.C.
2 CONT February 6, 1868
2 CONT In the 83rd year of her age
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY - THE GEORGETOWN COURIER, MARRIAGE AND DEATH NOTICES, 1865-1876 by Wesley E. Pippinger, p. 20
2 CONT DIED.BRONAUGH - 6th inst., in her 83rd year, Mrs. Anne E. Bronaugh, widow of the late John W. Bronaugh, of Stafford co.,Va.  She was the daughter of Col. Daniel and Sarah McCarty, of Cedar Grove, and the granddaughter of Col. Dani
2 CONC el McCarty, of Mt. Air, and Col. George Mason, of Gunston Hall, Fairfax Co.,VA.  Both her grandfathers were of Revolutionary memory. (15 Feb 1868)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  She is listed on the 1850 census of Georgetown, Wash., D.C. living with her son, John W. Bronaugh and his wife Frances P.T. and her age was 64 and she would live 18 years more. - JMC
