2 CONT Spencer Ball b. "Coan", Northumberland Co, VA Aug. 6, 1762
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - VIRGINIA LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson, p. 115
2 CONT Col. Spencer Ball married Elizabeth Landon Carter 27 March 1788.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Died "Portici", Prince William Co. Feb. 28, 1832; will proved 4 June 1832 Prince Wm. Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT PRINCE WILLIAM CO., VA. BURIAL INDEX 1800-1993 by Ronald Ray Turner
2 CONT Ball, Spencer 6 Aug. 1762 - 28 Feb 1832 - Ball Cemetery - Portici.
2 CONT (now owned by the Federal government as part of the Manassas battlefield - JMC)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spencer Ball (1762-1801) purchased the 762 acre estate of Portici from his
2 CONT wife's brother, George Carter.  The home which was also known as Portici was
2 CONT built on the estate for Elizabeth Landon (Carter) Ball.  One account states
2 CONT that her husband, Spencer Ball built it for her, while another says that it was built for her by her father, Robert "Councillor" Carter.  At any rate, this first Portici was a large brick-gabled mansion and was situated on a steep
2 CONC  hill toward the west - a beautiful estate with terraces in front where the flowers and vegetables were placed.  Entirely destroyed by fire, supposedly after the Second Battle of Manassas, Portici's glory is but a memory.  VIRGINI
2 CONC A LINEAGES, LETTERS & MEMORIES by Alice Jean Nelson, p. 5
2 CONT
2 CONT NATIONAL INTELLIGENCER & WASHINGTON ADVERTISER NEWSPAPERS ABSTRACTS 1800-1805 by Joan M. Dixon, p. 93
2 CONT In Chancery, State of MD.:  Chas. Carroll of Carrollton, Nicholas Carroll, Daniel Carroll of Duddington, Wm Smith, Abraham Vanbibber & Isaac Vanbibber vs. Spencer Ball and Betsey Landon Ball of VA.
