2 CONC Boone, in the military organization known as Howard's Rangers. These brothers were Milton, Lindsay, Martrom, John and Samuel Lewis. Judge Martrom D. Lewis of St. Louis, a son of the Martrom named above, is authority for the statem
2 CONC ent (made in 1905) that five of the brothers (including his father) participated with Boone in the War of 1812. Some of these Lewis brothers, if not all, were with Captain Nathan Boone (Daniel Morgan's brother) in the night battle
