2 CONC ed by Colonel John Shaw, founder of Pike county's first seat of justice at Coles' Grove, who was scouting for the Rangers and was with Boone's party in this encounter. One of the Lewis brothers in this battle was said to have been
2 CONC  wounded by an Indian arrow. In Missouri history it is recorded that one of the brothers came home from the war with arrow wounds.
