1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Creswell (* around 1772 in South Carolina ; †  11 September 1850 in Eutaw, Alabama ) was an American politician. Between 1814 and 1816 he was Lieutenant Governor of South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Creswell spent most of his life in the Laurens District in South Carolina. There he practiced law. Politically, he was a member of the Federalist Party. Later, he joined the Democratic-Republican Party.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1798 he was elected to the House of Representatives of South Carolina. In 1802, his candidacy failed as a federalist for the House of Representatives of the United States. In 1814, he was elected Lieutenant Governor of his stat
2 CONC e by the South Carolina General Assembly. He held this office between December 10, 1814, and December 5, 1816. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He then served as the Comptroller General of South Carolina, where he was elected in 1816. He later became a candidate for the appointment of an appellate judge and as president of the Bank of South Carolina . Creswell rejected bo
2 CONC th functions and retired as a lawyer. He died on September 11, 1850, in Eutaw.
