1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://germannafamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I108613&tree=tree1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Winneford Rector, 1756 - 1949, was the daughter of Daniel Rector and Nancy Ann Oldham.  . "Died in her 93rd year of her age"
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Ross, son of William Ross and Arminella Whiteside, in 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Lawrence, William, Nancy, Elizabeth, Presley, John, Mariah, Charles, Susan and Elijah
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT Married at age 30; resided on farm now known as the north farm of Geo. W. BERRY. Built 1st frame house in 1812. Desc. by Wm. HALLER of  medium stature but wonderful strength and endurance
2 CONT
2 CONT Old Settlers & Recent Inhabitants of German Township "20th Century History of Springfield, and Clark County, Ohio" William M. Rockel, 1908. Extracted 2002 by Jane M. Whitty. William Ross settled in Clark County, Ohio in 1798. Wife
2 CONC  was Winifred Rector, sister of Charles Rector. 8 children/7 b. in KY: William, Elijah (left twp 1825), Nancy, Elizabeth, John(see below), Presley (d. 1852), Mary, Charles (b. in OH). Son-in-Law: Daniel HARR of Urbana. from Mason 
2 CONC Co, KY but not native of there.>Warren Co, OH (1 year)>Tremont. 
2 CONT
