2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=marcwheat&id=I04031
2 CONT * * 1845 Will: Daniel Rector's will was probated Oct 5, 1845 in Delaware Co. Indiana. On file with the Archives and Special Collections, Bracken Library, Ball State University, Muncie, Indiana.
2 CONT * * *  "Testimony of Samuel Hutchings & Jonathan B. Arnold two of the subscribing witnesses to the last will and testament of Daniel Rector late of Delaware County Indiana deceased... Do you know the time of his death as near as m
2 CONC ay be the day and month of his death. Answer upon the morning of the eleventh day of Sept AD 1845..."
2 CONT * * Biographical History of Page County, Iowa, (Chicago: Lewis & Dunbar, Publishers, 1890), 745-746: JAMES SAUNDERS [sic, "Sanders"], one of the representative farmers of Nebraska Township, was born in Rockcastle County, Kentucky,
2 CONC  August 8, 1818, and is the son of Abednego and Amy (Cook) Saunders, natives of North Carolina... He was married January 23, 1840, to Miss Phoebe Rector, a daughter of '''Daniel''' and Nancy (Garber) Rector. She was born September
2 CONC  22, 1820, in Clarke County, Ohio."
