1 NAME Daingerfield /Lewis/
2 GIVN Daingerfield
2 SURN Lewis
2 _MARNM Lewis
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 JUL 1785
2 PLAC Marmion Ln
2 ADDR
3 CITY King George
3 STAE VA
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 SEP 1862
2 ADDR
3 CITY King George
3 STAE VA
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/35861594/daingerfield-lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT Daingerfield Lewis, of "Marmion", King George Co., Va.; son of George Washington Lewis (1757-1821) and Catherine Daingerfield (1764-1820); born July 14, 1785; died Sept. 18, 1862; married Sep. 10, 1807 in Spotsylvania Co., Va., Lu
2 CONC cy, born 1787, daughter of Thomas Pratt and Jane Brockenbrough. They resided at Marmion throughout their lives, and had twelve children. Lucy Brockenbrough Lewis, died 16th August 1856 — aged 69 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT * 1. Fielding Lewis, born Oct. 15, 1808, m. (1) his first cousin, Catherine Daingerfield Lewis (1820-1849), daughter of Samuel Lewis and Sarah Attaway Miller, with whom he had two children. Fielding Lewis married (2) Mary Imogen G
2 CONC reen, daughter of John and Ann (Forrest) Green of Georgetown, District of Columbia and had seven children.
2 CONT * 2. Jane Brockenbrough Lewis, b. Sep. 20, 1810, m. her cousin, George Washington Lewis of "Claymont" Westmoreland county, son of Samuel Lewis and Sarah Attaway Miller.
2 CONT * 3. Catherine Daingerfield Lewis, b. Jan. 16, 1812, m. Col. Thomas B. Barbour of "Spy Hill", King George county, Va.
2 CONT * 4. Betty Washington Lewis, b. Jan. 16, 1814, m. William Alexander D. G. Ashton of King George County.
2 CONT * 5. Susan Lewis, b. July 16, 1816, Sep. 20, 1818.
2 CONT * 6. Lucy Pratt Lewis, b. July 19, 1818, d. 1876; m. Dr. Michael Wallace, born in Va., Nov. 14, 1817; died Oct. 14, 1877, son of Gustavus Brown and Frances (Lurty) Wallace. They resided at "White Hall", King George, Va.
2 CONT * 7. Susan Lewis, b. 1820, d. Sep. 8, 1821.
2 CONT * 8. Maj. George Washington Lewis, C.S.A., b. Feb. 17, 1823, d. Aug. 2, 1862 (KIA), never married.
2 CONT * 9. Mary Willis Lewis, b. Feb. 21, 1824, d. 1885; m. 1855 Col. John Tayloe (b. Oct. 18, 1818) of Chatterton, Va., son of Lieut. John Tayloe, U.S.N. She was his second wife, and had four children.
2 CONT * 10. Samuel Lewis, b. Mar. 21, 1825, died in infancy.
2 CONT * 11. Henry Byrd Lewis, b. July 17, 1826, d. 1917; m. (1) 1849 Ellen Coleman Dickinson (1830-1892), by whom he had four children; m. (2) Lena R. Fairfax, no issue.
2 CONT * 12. Attaway Miller Lewis, b. "Marmion", King George, Va., Mar. 3, 1829, died unmarried in 1915.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT
2 CONT * “Lewis of Warner Hall: The History of a Family, Including the Genealogy of ...” Page 179.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=yeWgvfDpwbwC&lpg=PA126&vq=Baylis&pg=PA179#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] 
2 CONT
2 CONT * ”Lewis Family of Warner Hall.” The William and Mary Quarterly, vol. 10, no. 1, 1901, pp. 48–54. JSTOR, http://www.jstor.org/stable/1919805. Accessed 28 Feb. 2021. NOTE: This article was continued from Volume IX of the journal, p
2 CONC .259; quote given here is from page 3 of 7.
2 CONT * [https://livesandlegaciesblog.org/2015/09/18/meet-the-lewis-family-george-lewis/ “ Meet the Lewis Family: George Lewis”]  SEPTEMBER 18, 2015 / FERRYFARMANDKENMORE
2 CONT * Page 119 of "Genealogies of the Lewis and kindred families, ed. by John Meriwether McAllister and Lura Boulton Tandy."
2 CONT *https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/35861594/daingerfield-lewis
