1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 209
2 CONT Lorenzo Lewis was born about 1804.  He was 43 years if age when he died in 1847 which would make his birth about 1804 and he was born at "Woodlawn" in Fairfax Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Esther Maria Coxe of Philadelphia, daughter of Dr. John Redman Coxe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son, Lorenzo Lewis, after his marriage, lived at Audley and operated the farm near Berryville, Clarke Co.,VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Lorenzo Lewis and other members of his family are buried in the Episcopal Churchyard in Berryville.
2 CONT
2 CONT The names of the 6 sons of Lorenzo and his wife, Esther, were:  George Washington Lewis, John Redman Coxee Lewis, Lawrence Fielding Lewis, Edward Parke Custis Lewis, Charles Conrad Lewis and H. L. Daingerfield Lewis.  John Redman 
2 CONC and Lawrence Fielding were twins.  Three of these six sons are buried near their parents in Berryville:  Lawrence Fielding who died at Audley in 1857 in his 23rd year; Charles Conrad who died at the University of Virginia in 1859,
2 CONC  aged 19; and H. L. Daingerfield, born April 25, 1841, who died December 17, 1893. - Ibid
