1 NOTE !BIRTH - THE WASHINGTONS AND THEIR HOMES by John W. Wayland, p. 223
2 CONT John Augustine Washington, II, born in Westmoreland Co.,VA in 1789, was a son of Corbin and his wife Hannah Lee and thus a grandson of John Augustine Washington, I, the General's second full brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT He married Jane Charlotte Blackburn in 1814.  She was a daughter of Capt. Richard Scott Blackburn and his wife, Judith Ball.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid p. 225
2 CONT John Augustine Washington, II, like his brother Richard Henry Lee, was short-lived even for a Washington.  He died at the age of 43.  We may be pretty certain that his health was poor for 10 years before his death, for he made his
2 CONC  will on Aug. 6, 1822, when he was only 33, and just a year or 2 after he had finished his mansion house at Blakeley.
2 CONT
2 CONT GENIUS OF LIBERTY 1817-1843 by M. Hiatt, A. Hennings & P.B. Duncan, p. 75
2 CONT Died on the 14th inst. at Mt. Vernon in the 43rd year of his age, John A. Washington, Esq., proprietor of that estate.
