1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/243164776/anna-maria-thornton Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 29 2023, 19:33:45 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/243164776/anna_maria_thornton
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Maria Washington (1788-1816) married in 1810, her third cousin Capt. Reuben Thornton (1780-1815). They settled in Wilkinson County, Miss. Their sons were Dr. Churchill Jones (1811-45) who married in 1840, Lucy Maria Beverley 
2 CONC (c1823-97); and Charles Augustine Thornton (1813-86) who married in 1839, Cornelia Virginia Randolph (1819-49).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt. George Augustine Washington (c1758-93) served in the Revolutionary War. He married in 1785, Frances Bassett (1767-96), daughter of Col. Burwell Bassett, of Eltham, New Kent County, Va. and niece of Martha Washington. Their fou
2 CONC r children were George Fayette (1787); Anna Maria (1788-1816); George Fayette (1790-1867) who married in 1813, Maria Frame (1793-1860), of Charles Town, [W.]Va.; and Charles Augustine Washington (1791-1811)(unm.) who died in Cadiz
2 CONC , Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Albert Welles, The Pedigree and History of the Washington Family (New York, 1879), 186-187; John W. Wayland, The Washingtons and Their Homes (Genealogical Pub., 1944), 323; John B. Burke, Burke's Presidential Families of the U
2 CONC nited States (London, 1975), 63; Dr. Justin M. Glenn, The Washingtons, A Family History, Volume One, Seven Generations of the Presidential Branch (Savas Beatie, El Dorado Hills, Ca. 2014), I: 91, 198, 204, 447; James Houston Barr 
2 CONC III, Lt. Colonel Nathaniel Pope, c1610-1660, of Virginia, Ancestor of Washington, Governors and Legislators, History of His Descendants (Louisville, Ky. 2018), 27.
