1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A064865  DAR Ancestor #: A064865] 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Kenner Family" - The William and Mary Quarterly, Vol. 14, No. 3 (Jan., 1906), pp. 173-181 (see attached
2 CONT
2 CONT RODHAM4 KENNER (Richard,3 Rodham,2 Richard') was probably Col. Rodham Kenner, scholar at William and Mary  College in 1760, burgess for Northumberland county in 1773,  member of the State Convention in 1776, and one of the signers
2 CONC  of the Westrnoreland address February 1776; county lieutenant in 1785. He married in 1763 Elizabeth Plater, daughter of George Plater, Esq., (marriage bond-Quarterly VII. 191.)
2 CONT
