1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Veteran - War of 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT George Lewis Ball served as a Lieutenant in Major Crutchfield's Detachment. His service records may be found at the National Archives in roll box number nine, record 2105. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The Society of the War of 1812 in the Commonwealth of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT George Lewis Ball was born on 7 March 1790, and died in 1874.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a schoolteacher after the war.
2 CONT
2 CONT George was married to Catherine "Kitty" Kerfoot (1794-1870) on 12 Nov 1816. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial is in the Ball-Shumate Cemetery located on tax map number 6982- 35 - 2573 in Fauquier County, VA. 
2 CONT
