1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Benjamin W. Graves''' was the s/o Thomas Graves who applied for a Revolutionary War pension while living in Russell Co., KY. Thomas served as a private from Louisa Co., VA, in the company commanded by Captain Ph
2 CONC illips in the Virginia line for 9 months, Revolutionary War Pension Papers, W1418; Certificate of Pension issued 17 Aug 1833. Benjamin W. Graves' mother was Mary Chilton. 
