1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:  The Dodson Book Allan went to Davidson Co., TN where he bought land near the Hermitage from Philip Wilson in Sept 1813.  Apparently his first wife died there and he returned to Pittsylvania Co. where he rema
2 CONC rried, and then returned to Tennessee.  According to the Frank D. Fuller manuscript, Allan had two daughters by his first wife, and two children by the second wife. A descendant has written that Allan Dodson died in 1823 "along th
2 CONC e road" while moving his family from Kentucky to Tennessee.  His son wrote many years later that he has searched unsuccessfully for his father's grave.  Allan's known children are Nancy Dodson, LydiaDodson, American Dodson, and By
2 CONC rd Granville Dodson.  There was also a Mary Dodson listed in court records with Allan's other children in1851 but it is unclear if she was another daughteror if they were referring to his second wife.  Nancy and Lydia were by the 
2 CONC first wife and Byrd by the second.  Records differ on which wife was the mother of America Dodson and, of course, Mary Dodson.
