1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Another source says he was born in Trimble County, Kentucky. 
2 CONT       The 1830 Hardin County, Kentucky, census lists Thomas Reno, 2 males under 5, 1 male 15 to 20, 1 male 20 to 30, 1 male 70 to 80, 1 female under 5, and 1 female 20 to 30. 
2 CONT       The 1840 Hardin County, Kentucky, census lists Thomas Reno, 1 male under 5, 1 male 5 to 10, 1 male 10 to 15, 1 female under 5, 1 female 5 to 10, 1 female 15 to 20, and 1 female 30 to 40. 
2 CONT       The 1850 Hardin County, Kentucky, census lists Thomas Reno, 45 b. KY; Letitia, 38 b. KY; Emeline, 22 b. KY; Siomy, male, 20 b. KY; Lucy, 18 b. KY; Christopher, 16 b. KY; Elizabeth, 14 b. KY; and Letitia, 11 b. KY. 
2 CONT       The 1870 Daviess County, Missouri, census lists Thomas P. Reno, 58 b. KY, farmer; Eliz., 56 b. TN; and Alexander Wood, 10 b. IL. 
2 CONT       [Steve Fancy research] Thomas Reno and Charles C. Reno signed a marriage bond of fifty pounds for Thomas' marriage to Letitia Linder on November 24, 1825 in Hardin Co., KY. They both spelled their name Reno.  http://familytr
2 CONC eemaker.genealogy.com/users/d/a/m/Sue-Reneau-Damewood/BOOK-0001/0004-0041.html#CHILD198
