1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Francis Lucinda Reno Hawkins 
2 CONT BIRTH	1 Jan 1817 Muhlenberg County, Kentucky, USA 
2 CONT DEATH	27 May 1845 (aged 28) Palmyra, Marion County, Missouri, USA 
2 CONT BURIAL	Unknown, Specifically: Marion County, Pallymra, Missouri
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/48074740
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Francis is the male spelling, Frances is the female spelling
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Lucinda Reno was the daughter of Lewis W. Reno and Mary Lucinda "Polly" Shropshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married: Strother Moses Hawkins on 20 Dec 1832 in Marion County, Palymra, Mo. (She was his first wife and he remarried three more times.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were: Mary Francis Hawkins,  James S. Hawkins,  James William Hawkins, Hulda Elizabeth Hawkins, Joseph H. Hawkins, Strother Moses Hawkins, Jr., Elizabeth Jane Hawkins, and Samuel Hawkins
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT aka Fanney, Fanny, Fannie in various records
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Francis is the male spelling, Frances is the female spelling.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd Wife- Strother Moses Hawkins married Frances Jane McGrady on 17 Dec 1857 in Fannin County, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were: Laura Jane Hawkins, Newton Eldridge Hawkins, Sarah Ashley Hawkins,  Randolph Hawkins
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Sandra Fuller Fihser, sampsfaol.com, a descendent of Lucinda Reno, says that Lucinda was the daughter of Lewis Reno and Mary Lucinda Shropshire, and the wife of Strother Moses Hawkins.  The 1850 census for Fannin Co., TX showe
2 CONC d S.M. Hawkins 41 born in VA; James 17 Mo; Hulda E. 15 MO; S.M. 12 MO; James S. 10 MO; J.C. 8 MO; E.G. 6 MO; M.F. 4 MO; and S.R. 2 TX.  Also in Fannin Co., in 1850 is Andrew Bird Hawkins 45 VA, his wife Eliza 38 KY (nee Elizabeth 
2 CONC Reno), and 5 children:  Juleann 14 MO; James A. 10 MO; Cynthia C. 9 MO; Lucinda A. 4 TX; and Mary M. 1 TX.  This suggests that Srother and his brother Andrew married the Reno sisters in Missouri, and then moved their families to F
2 CONC annin Co., TX between 1845 and 1847 after Frances Lucinda died.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Reno/Reneau source.
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT Seems to have died while giving birth to her last child, Mary Frances (born same day as her death, 27 May 1845).
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT 9FQZ-C62  Lucinda in entry for Sam Hawkins, "Texas Deaths, 1890-1976"  "Texas Deaths, 1890-1976," database with images, <i>FamilySearch</i> (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:K3SR-YDF : 13 March 2018), Lucinda in entry for S
2 CONC am Hawkins, 17 Feb 1919; citing certificate number 7421, State Registrar Office, Austin; FHL micr  https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:K3SR-YDF
