1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Aurelius_Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=6865432
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Aurelius "Mark" Smith (January 24, 1851[b] – April 7, 1924) was an American attorney and politician who served eight terms as Arizona Territorial Delegate to Congress and as one of the first two Senators from Arizona. As a 
2 CONC Delegate he was a leader in the effort to gain statehood for Arizona. His non-voting status however minimized his influence with only 35 of the 277 bills he introduced into the House of Representatives being signed into law.[1] La
2 CONC ck of a voice in the United States Senate further weakened his efforts as he managed to get Arizona statehood bills passed by the House only to see the legislation blocked in the Senate.[2] Beyond his efforts for statehood, Smith 
2 CONC worked to have government buildings constructed and to provide relief to his constituents affected by either man-made or natural misfortunes. His efforts to provide relief to the citizens of Arizona did not however extend to the i
2 CONC ndigenous population for whom Smith expressed great animosity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Smith was a dedicated conservative for most of his political career. This changed following his electoral defeat in 1908. As Smith campaigned to become one of Arizona's first two Senators he became a progressive. In this new role 
2 CONC he was a firm supporter of Woodrow Wilson's New Freedom initiatives.
