1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Lexington Weekly Intelligencer, April 24, 1897
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATHS
2 CONT
2 CONT Died, at Odessa, April 20, 1897, of heart failure, Mr. William D. McHatton, aged 68 years. Interment at Greenton cemetery, April 20.
2 CONT
2 CONT This death was very sudden and was a great shock to his relatives and friends. A Few minutes before his heath he was in the best of health and had been doing his morning chores and after performing them he went into the house and 
2 CONC there the fatal spell came on without any warning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. McHatton was born in Kentucky and immigrated to this state while young and has spent the greater part of his life in this county. Shortly after Odessa was built he removed from Greenton to that city and has always since been n
2 CONC umbered as one of her foremost citizens. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Christian church and has ever been found performing every good work in the up building of the cause of Christ. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He leaves a brother, Mr. Harvey McHatton, of Spokane, Wash., a devoted wife, two sons, Messer's James Z. and Bowdry, who reside in Odessa, and a host of friends to mourn his death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT We extend our sympathy to the sorrowing relatives and numerous friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
