2 NOTE Lt. General Richard S. Ewell (CSA) ("Old Bald Head") is my 14th cousin four times removed.
2 NOTE At Gettysburg he failed to take advantage of the situation by capturing Cemetery Hill after being given discretionary orders by General Robert E. Lee. Unlike Jackson before him, he required exact instructions. He fought at the Wil
3 CONC derness where the same problem developed. At Spotsylvania, one of his divisions was all but destroyed. At the "Bloody Angle," he fell from his horse incapacitating him and forcing him to temporarily relinquish command but Lee made
3 CONC  it permanent. He was given command defending Richmond and was captured at Sayler's Creek on April 6, 1865, during the retreat to Appomattox. He was sent to Fort Warren, Massachusetts, and was released on August 19, 1865.
