1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From his obituary in the Evening Bulletin of Maysville, Kentucky, of Aug. 23, 1895:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin Clifton Foxworthy
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin Clifton Foxworthy, of Mt. Carmel, who had been ill the past month, died Sunday night, Aug. 18th, aged 86 years. He leaves a large circle of friends and relatives:
2 CONT *one son, John William Foxworthy, and
2 CONT *one sister, Mrs. Matt B. Tolle, of this city.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, who was Miss Sallie DeBell, died nine years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man who by his walk and conversation bore out the Master's teaching, and in his death the church loses an earnest and effective worker. He was a pulpit orator off no mean power and the high esteem in which he was held by 
2 CONC all who knew him evidenced the great worth of the man. A leader has gone from us to enjoy the eternal reward which he has earned and which Christ has promised those who are faithful until the end.
