1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT From The (Maysville, KY) Public Ledger of Thursday, May 12, 1898:
2 CONT
2 CONT Yesterday's Harvest: Two Venerable Mason County Residents Pass Away at Their Homes
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Elizabeth Berry, wife of Mr. Enoch Berry, died at 6 o'clock yesterday morning at her home at Lewisburg, aged 61.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased was a most estimable lady, and her death will be mourned by scores of relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband and ten children survive:
2 CONT *Prof. W. T. of this city.
2 CONT *B C. of Mayslick
2 CONT *J. A. of Vinita, I.T.
2 CONT *Mrs. Thomas Gaither of Lewisburg
2 CONT *Enoch of Parson, Kansas
2 CONT *Mrs. J. H. Bolinger of Oklahoma City, O.T.
2 CONT *Messrs. Charles and
2 CONT *Ed, and
2 CONT *Misses Mamie and
2 CONT *Lizzie at home.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will take place tomorrow afternoon at 3 o'clock from the Baptist Church at Lewisburg with services by the Rev. M. B. Adams of Frankfort.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment in the Cemtery at the Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral of Mrs. Elizabeth Berry, mother of Professor W. T. Berry, of this city, mention of whose death at Lewisburg was made yesterday, will occur tomorrow afternoon at 3 o'clock from the Lewisburg Baptist Church, services by 
2 CONC Rev. M. B. Adams, of Frankfort. Interment at the Lewisburg burying grounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From The (Maysville, KY) Public Ledger of Friday, May 13, 1898:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ledger yesterday, in noticing the death of Mrs. Elizabeth Berry, made the unfortunate mistake of saying that her husband survived. Mr. Berry, who was one of the best citizens of our county, died some 10 years since.
