1 NOTE !BIRTH - Tombstone
2 CONT Gives his date of birth as August 11, 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA MARRIAGE LICENSES, 1811-1858 by Wesley Pippenger,
2 CONT p. 66
2 CONT BRONAUGH, John W. & BRONAUGH, Frances P.T. Sep 01 1841.
2 CONT INDEX TO MARRIAGES & DEATHS IN THE (BALTIMORE) SUN 1837-1850 by Thomas L.
2 CONT Hollowak, p. 67
2 CONT Bronaugh, John W., 2 Sept 1841, Frances P. T. Bronaugh, dau. of John
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - THE GEORGETOWN COURIER MARRIAGE AND DEATH NOTICES 1865-1876 by Wesley E. Pippenger, p. 124
2 CONT DIED BRONAUGH - July 21, 1874 at 5:45 o'clock p.m., in the sixtieth year of his age, John W. Bronaugh, eldest son of the late John W. and Annie E. Bronaugh, of Stafford Co.,VA. (25 Jul 1874)
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid
2 CONT He is buried in Congressional Cemetery, Washington, D.C., Range 42, Site 152
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 census of Georgetown, Washington, D.C., p. 152, Dwelling #70,
2 CONT Family #70 lists John W. Bronaugh as head of family working as a clerk in U.S. Government office.  Frances P. T. Bronaugh is evidently his wife and Hamilton Bronaugh must be their son.  Ann E. Bronaugh must be John W.'s mother, An
2 CONC ne Eilbeck McCarty Bronaugh.  Martha Henderson is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bronaugh, John W.         36   b/VA
2 CONT                 Frances P.T.   35     VA
2 CONT                   Hamilton        2   Georgetown
2 CONT Henderson, Martha          50     VA
2 CONT Bronaugh, Ann E.            64     VA
2 CONT Note:  See 1880 census of Frances P. T. Bronaugh. - JMC
