1 NOTE !BIRTH - DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA DEATH RECORDS AUG. 1, 1874 TO JULY 31, 1879 P. 36
2 CONT Bronaugh, Sarah M. 60 years old when she died in 1875 which would make her
2 CONT birth about 1815 prob. in Georgetown.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Tombstone
2 CONT Sarah Marie Bronaugh, 2nd daughter of John W. and Anne E. Bronaugh died in Georgetown Nov. 20, 1875.
2 CONT Tombstone reads:
2 CONT Sacred to the Memory of
2 CONT SARAH MARIA BRONAUGH
2 CONT 2nd Dau. of John W. & Anne E. Bronaugh
2 CONT Who Died in Georgetown,D.C.
2 CONT Nov. 20th 1875
2 CONT Note:  She is listed on same tombstone as sister Margaret. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - RECORDS OF CONGRESSIONAL CEMETERY, WASHINGTON, D.C.
2 CONT Sarah M. Bronaugh was buried 23 Nov 1875 in Congressional Cemetery, Washington, D.C. Range 42, Site #150.
2 CONT Note:  She was sister of John W. Bronaugh and is buried in his lot. - JMC
2 CONT
2 CONT INTERMENTS IN THE HISTORIC CONGRESSIONAL CEMETERY - OBITUARY
2 CONT Bronaugh, Sarah M.       d. 20 Nov 1875           60 yrs
2 CONT Bronaugh.  On the 20th inst.  In the 61st year of her age, Miss S. M. Bronaugh.  Her funeral will take place from the residence of her sister, Mrs. John W. Bronaugh, No. 44 Market Street, Georgetown at 12 o'clock on Tuesday the 23
2 CONC rd inst.  The friends of the family are invited to attend (Baltimore and Richmond papers please copy.)
2 CONT
2 CONT BOYD'S DIRECTORY OF WASHINGTON, GEORGETOWN & ALEXANDRIA 1870
2 CONT S. M. Bronaugh, clerk 2d Comptroller, 55 2nd, Georgetown
2 CONT Note:  She is living at same location as H. Bronaugh (Hambleton) and they are working in same office. - JMC
