1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_H._Roane
2 CONT
2 CONT William Henry Roane (September 17, 1787 – May 11, 1845) was a politician from Virginia. He was the son of Judge Spencer Roane and the grandson of founding father Patrick Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Virginia, Roane pursued in preparatory studies as a young man. He was a member of the Virginia House of Delegates from 1812 to 1815 and was later elected a Democratic-Republican to the United States House of Representative
2 CONC s in 1814, serving from 1815 to 1817. Roane was not a candidate for reelection and instead became a member of the executive council of Virginia. He was later elected a Democrat to the United States Senate to fill a vacancy, servin
2 CONC g from 1837 to 1841. Their, he was chairman of the Committee on the District of Columbia from 1837 to 1839. After being unsuccessful for reelection, Roane engaged in agricultural pursuits until his death on May 11, 1845 in Tree Hi
2 CONC ll, Virginia. He was interred at Lyons Family Cemetery in Hanover County, Virginia.
