2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1841
2 PLAC Marengo, Alabama, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Spencer Roane's parentage remains a mystery. In my South Louisiana branch of the Roane family it has long been understood that we are descended from the Roanes of King and Queen County Virginia, whose émigré progen
2 CONC itor was Charles Roane, son of Robert of Chaldon, Surrey. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Many editions of the William & Mary Quarterly show that the Roane family of Virginia was large, with lots of children in successive generations. Other parental relationships in the family are made clear through exhaustive document
2 CONC ation, but it seems there's no record of this Spencer child being born in 1798. In 1959 my great aunt commissioned an extensive genealogy of the Roane family to answer that question, and that genealogist was unable to find an answ
2 CONC er. What we know is that Spencer Roane was born in King and Queen County, Virginia in 1798 (not to be confused with Judge Spencer Roane, born in 1762), and died in Marengo, Alabama in 1841.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a 1938 article about the Roane family in the William and Mary Quarterly, The Roanes of King and Queen and King William Counties by Elizabeth Hawes Ryland, records from those counties were lost over time: "Owing to los
2 CONC s of records, King William and King and Queen are among our neglected counties. With the passing of each generation more and more of the rich store of unrecorded tradition and homely lore of these counties is lost to the living."
2 CONT
2 CONT For a variety of reasons, my best guess is that he came from the family of Thomas Roane of Newington. If anyone has documented information on Spencer Roane's birth (presumably in 1798 in King and Queen County), please help solve t
2 CONC he mystery.
2 CONT
2 CONT W. LaSalle
2 CONT January 2025
