1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~kywolfe/wpic173.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been to town while he was living in Kentucky and he always rode his favorite horse. He got a $20.00 gold piece while he was in town. He didn't leave for home until after dark and when he arrived at a small ravine he had to 
2 CONC cross there was a man waiting for him. He hollered, "Give me that $20.00 gold piece or I'll shoot." My mother said, "What did you do?" Uncle Andy answered, "I hit my mare hard and she jumped the ditch and ran on into the dark, I k
2 CONC new he was just as liable to miss me as hit me in the dark!"
2 CONT
2 CONT This Andrew Jackson Spencer was the one for whom Big Andy Ridge was named. A Kentucky newspaper article says, "The community was named to honor Andy Spencer, an outstanding area leader whose tremendous proportions in size resulted
2 CONC  in the appellation "Big Andy". http://www.miles-shute-kouns-families.com/getperson.php?personID=I2692&tree=F 
