2 DATE AFT 1794
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary was born about 1770. She was the daughter of James Tapscott. She passed away after 1794.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Thomas Hammond was married first to Mary Lewis “Polly” Tapscott, the daughter of James Tapscott and Susannah Baker of Lancaster Co., Virginia. Polly’s mother’s parents were John Baker and Judith Wood of near Charles Town, and Pol
2 CONC ly’s uncle was John Baker, a well known attorney in Shepherdstown. Polly’s brother Baker Tapscott was a merchant of Shepherdstown and near Sharpsburg, Maryland. Thomas Hammond and Polly Tapscott’s marriage license was issued in La
2 CONC ncaster Co., Virginia on 6 Nov 1792.71 Polly died after 10 Jun 1794 when she signed a deed with her husband Thomas Hammond to convey a Charles Town lot to John Young."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Ailes, Jane E. Ailes. "Study of the Enslaved at Happy Retreat: The Washington and Hammond Era, 1747-1837. Slavery-at-Happy-Retreat-1747-1837-final-version-Jul-2024.pdf.
