2 CONC sued land warrants for 400 acres of land in Washington Co., Tenn. in 1782; h e did not stay in Ten. and moved to the Pendleton District, S. C. and appears in the 1790 cen sus there. (339 James McAdams - 400) The census of 1790 sho
2 CONC ws that he owned no slaves but b y 1800 he had acquired six, which was a large number for that area at this time. In 1802, 180 3 and 1804 he purchased lands on Crooked Creek, a branch of the Saluda River. Is listed i n the 1810 ce
