1 NOTE {geni:about_me} One source states in regards to Churchill Downs...."The track is named for John and Henry Churchill, who leased 80 acres of land to their nephew, Col. https://www.geni.com/people/Meriwether-Clark-Jr/600000000966359
2 CONC 6220?through=6000000000590560934 (grandson of explorer https://www.geni.com/people/William-Clark/6000000031113438993?through=6000000009663007731). Clark was president of the Louisville Jockey Club and Driving Park Association, whi
2 CONC ch formed in 1874.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.americasbestracing.net/tracks/churchill-downs
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia states "It officially opened in 1875 and was named for Samuel Churchill, whose family was prominent in Kentucky for many years."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Churchill_Downs
