2 CONT Mary Iredell was born in Barren Co., Ky. and died of Cholera between June 1st-August 1st, 1833 at the Lunatic Asylum. No place of burial was given. She was most likely buried in an unmarked grave on the grounds Eastern State Hospi
2 CONC tal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1833 Cholera Deaths by 2006 by Pam Brinegar
2 CONT
2 CONT By Cholera, in the CITY OF LEXINGTON, from the 1st of June to the 1st of August, as reported to the City Council by a committee appointed for that purpose, consisting of Messrs. Leavy, Layton, M'Kinney & Gough. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The Kentucky Reporter [Lexington, Fayette, Kentucky], 22 August 1833, p. 1. Microfilm held by the Kentucky Room, Lexington Public Library, Lexington. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Randolph Brooke Spotswood Iredale was the daughter of Judge Alexander Elliott and Elizabeth Alexander Lewis Spotswood of Glasgow, Barren County, Kentucky born between 1800-1805 Glasgow, Barren County, Kentucky She married Wil
2 CONC liam Henry Iredale Sept. 4, 1816 in Glasgow, KY. She was named after Her Aunt Mary Randolph Spotswood see memorial #26119426 married Judge Francis Taliaferro Brooke see memorial #26119063. 6 Children were born to William Henry and
2 CONC  Mary Spotswood Iredale, Elizabeth Iredale married Daniel Trigg Saunders or Sanders, Jane Mildred Iredale m. Reuben Henry Allen, Thornton Bushrod Iredale He settled in Lancaster Co. PA., Anna Maria Iredale m. John C. Knorpp they m
2 CONC oved to Germany, Alfred Spotswood Iredale he settled in San Francisco, CA., and Lucinda Iredale m. Winfield Scott of Nashville, TN.
