1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 8 children of Sarah Attaway Miller and Samuel Lewis:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Judge George Washington Lewis (1804 - 1879) m 1) Jane Brockenbrough Lewis, 6 children 2) Lucy Ann Robb, 2 children
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From FindaGrave 
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge George Washington Lewis was born 12 Nov 1803 at “Shellfield,” Colonial Beach, Virginia and died 6 April 1879 at “Claymont,” Westmoreland County, Virginia. The son of Samuel Lewis (1780-1840) and Sarah Attaway Miller (1785-18
2 CONC 22) and the grandson of George Lewis (1757 – 1821) and Catherine Daingerfield (1784-1820), and the great grandson of Fielding Lewis (1725-1781) and Betty Washington (1733-1797), he was educated at the University of Virginia. He wa
2 CONC s a lawyer and later a judge. He was also active in the life the Episcopal Church in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Lewis was married twice, once to Jane Brockenbrough Lewis (1810-1489) and second to Lucy Anne Robb (1823-1891). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had eight children. By his first wife he had 
2 CONT
2 CONT #Anna Louisa Lewis (1830-1897), 
2 CONT #Henry B. Lewis (1831- 1862 killed at the Battle of Seven Pines), 
2 CONT #Dr. Thomas M. Lewis (1833-1910),
2 CONT # Samuel Lewis (1836-1849), 
2 CONT #Robert Byrd Lewis (1841-1897), and 
2 CONT #Lucy Pratt Lewis Funsten (1844-1909). 
2 CONT
2 CONT By his second wife, he had two children 
2 CONT #Jane Vivian Lewis Long (1858-1931) and 
2 CONT #Alice Maria Lewis Wallace (1861-1960).
2 CONT
2 CONT His correspondence, which is now at the Special Collections at the University of Virginia, consist of letters from 1840 until his death in 1879 and documents his work as an attorney, a participant in the political life of Virginia
2 CONC , and includes letters from many notables in Virginia. He served in the Confederate Army as did his sons, Thomas, Robert, and Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * "Virginia Deaths and Burials, 1853-1912", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XRQQ-525 : 29 January 2020), Saml. Lewis in entry for Georg W. Lewis, 1879.
2 CONT *“Lewis of Warner Hall: The History of a Family, Including the Genealogy of ...” Page 159.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=yeWgvfDpwbwC&lpg=PA126&vq=Baylis&pg=PA159#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/sources/LZSS-2YW
2 CONT *https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9723389/george-washington-lewis “ Gravestone was placed by his granddaughter in the 20th century.”
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I113886&tree=Tree1
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *Info added @ Mary S Lockwood's "Lineage Book of the Charter Members" of the DAR
