1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Capt Henry Howell Lewis
2 CONT *BIRTH	7 Feb 1817 King George County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT *DEATH	17 Mar 1893 (aged 76) Baltimore, Baltimore City, Maryland, USA
2 CONT *BURIAL	 Loudon Park Cemetery Baltimore, Baltimore City, Maryland, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 children of Sarah Attaway Miller and Samuel Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Henry Howell Lewis, CSN (1817 - 1893), of Baltimore; m Ann Ogle Tayloe, 3 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexandria Gazette, March 18, 1893: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >A Relative of George Washington (St. Louis Republic). Captain Henry Howell Lewis who died in Baltimore on Friday last, was the last of General Washington’s grandnephews. He was the grandson of Colonel Fielding Lewis, who married 
2 CONC first Catherine and second Elizabeth, the one the cousin and the other the sister of General Washington. Captain Lewis was a descendant of the second marriage. He was appointed to the navy as a midshipman when very young under the
2 CONC  patronage of Henry Clay. A veteran of three wars, he enjoyed the esteem and respect of all who knew him, and he leaves to his surviving relatives a record in the public service and in private life worthy of the distinguished fami
2 CONC ly to which he belonged.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Forth Worth Gazette, March 23, 1893: Death of Capt. H.H. Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT >Capt. Henry Howell Lewis died yesterday at his home in Baltimore. Capt. Lewis was a great-grandnephew of George Washington. He was born in King George county, Va., in 1820. When eight years old he was, through the influence of He
2 CONC nry Clay, given the appointment of midshipman in the navy, and made his first cruise on the Constellation, now the practice ship at Annapolis. At the breaking out of the war he was on ordnance duty under Admiral Dahlgren at Washin
2 CONC gton. Resigning, he tendered his services to the Confederacy and participated in several engagements. At the close of the war he went to Baltimore and engaged in business. For the past eight years he had been an invalid. In 1845 C
2 CONC apt. Lewis was attacked with yellow fever and witnessed the death at his side of two of his shipmates. He attributed his later maladies to this attack. Capt. Lewis’s features were said to resemble those of Washington, as judged by
2 CONC  popular pictures. Capt. Lewis had placed in the Safe Deposit Company’s vault a sword which had been given by the great patriot to Major George Lewis, grandfather of Capt. Lewis. Capt. Lewis married Miss Ann Tayloe, daughter of Co
2 CONC l John Tayloe, of Mt. Airy, Va. Her death occurred some time ago. He leaves one daughter, two sons and three grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * San Francisco Call, Volume 87, Number 135, 14 April 1901. Page 1.  [https://cdnc.ucr.edu/cgi-bin/cdnc?a=d&d=SFC19010414.2.195.1&e=-------en--20--1--txt-txIN--------1 link] Mrs. Mann of Oakland will sell the sword of Washington” 
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/107459182/henry-howell-lewis
2 CONT *“Lewis of Warner Hall: The History of a Family, Including the Genealogy of ...” Page 159.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=yeWgvfDpwbwC&lpg=PA126&vq=Baylis&pg=PA159#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
