1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Fielding Lewis
2 CONT *BIRTH	15 Oct 1808
2 CONT *DEATH	15 Oct 1878 (aged 70)
2 CONT *BURIAL	 Marmion Cemetery, King George County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 children of Lucy Brockenbrough and Daingerfield Lewis:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/35836109/fielding-lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Fielding Lewis, born Oct. 15, 1808, m. (1) his first cousin, Catherine Daingerfield Lewis (1820-1849), daughter of Samuel Lewis and Sarah Attaway Miller, with whom he had two children. Fielding Lewis married (2) '''Mary Imogen
2 CONC  Green''', daughter of John and Ann (Forrest) Green of Georgetown, District of Columbia and had seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue (1):
2 CONT *1) Estelle Lewis, b. 1847, d. 1919, m. Capt. John Gray Pollock, C.S.A.
2 CONT *2) Catherine Daingerfield Lewis, b. 1849, d. Oct. 24, 1871, m. Matthew Bailey Pollock.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue (2):
2 CONT * 3) Annie Daingerfield Lewis, b. May 8, 1860, d. Nov. 22, 1943, m. William Cooper Dickinson (3ch).
2 CONT * 4) Attaway Maria Lewis, b. Feb. 4, 1862, d. Mar. 6, 1890, m. 1880 John Saunders Dickinson.
2 CONT * 5) Mary Imogen Lewis, b. Aug 19, 1864, d. Oct. 12, 1931, m. her cousin, Edgar Vivian Lewis of "Cleve", King George, Va.
2 CONT * 6) Fielding Lewis, Jr., b. Apr. 9, 1867, d. Nov. 12, 1908, m. Lydia "Lidey" Elliott.
2 CONT * 7) Mary Washington Lewis, b. Feb. 22, 1869, d. Nov. 9, 1892, unmarried.
2 CONT * 8) Helen Oscoala Lewis, b. 1870, m. her sister's widow, John Saunders Dickenson.
2 CONT * 9) Lucy Brockenbrough Lewis, b. Feb. 18, 1874, d. Nov. 18, 1963, m. Robert Carter Nicholas Grymes, Jr., son of Robert Carter Nicholas Grymes (1856-1924) and Martha Stuart Thornton Ashton (b. Mar. 5, 1858), of "Eagle's Nest", Kin
2 CONC g George County, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Fielding Lewis b Oct 15, 1808, inherited ‘Marmion’ from his father, Daingerfield Lewis (1785 - 1862).  His mother was Lucy Brockenbrough Pratt.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Info added @ Mary S Lockwood's "Lineage Book of the Charter Members" of the DAR
