1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Marriage to: Adam Empie II >SOURCE< Susan Taylor Block, Author
2 CONT  >SOURCE< Pedigree and History of the Washington Family by Albert Welles President American College for Genealogical Registry and Heraldry New York Society Library 1879
2 CONT
2 CONT a great granddaughter of Elizabeth (Betty) (Washington) Lewis [http://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Betty-Washington/6000000007409223684]
2 CONT
2 CONT a great, great niece of President George Washington [http://www.geni.com/people/George-Washington-1st-President-of-the-USA/6000000008211776777]
2 CONT
2 CONT member of: ''North Carolina Society of Colonial Dames''- >see Internet Source< Page 19 lists her membership [https://dcms.lds.org/view/action/ieViewer.do?dps_pid=IE586429&dps_dvs=1351855998858~760&dps_pid=IE586429&change_lng=en]
2 CONT
2 CONT about the 
2 CONT ===North Carolina Society of Colonial Dames===
2 CONT  [http://www.ncdames.org/refresh/templates/about.php?id=2]
2 CONT
2 CONT VENERABLE WOMAN DIES AT HOME IN WILMINGTON
2 CONT
2 CONT Was a Granddaughter of Bettie Washington, Only Sister of the First President of United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Special to Daily News)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilmington, June 19. Funeral services for Mrs. Virginia G. Empie, 88 years of age, a granddaughter of Betty Washington, only sister of George Washington, revolutionary leader and first President of the United States, whose death o
2 CONC ccurred rather suddenly Monday night following a brief illness, were conducted from St. James' Episcopal church, of which she had been a communicant for over 60 years, this afternoon at S o'clock and interment was made in the fami
2 CONC ly plot in Oakdale cemetery. The services were in charge of Rev. Duval L. Gwathmey, rector of the church, who recently came here from Norfolk. The church building was filled to overflowing with sorrowing friends and the flowers se
2 CONC nt are best described as a wilderness, so profuse and numerous were the offerings. Mrs. Empie was one of the best known women in Eastern Carolina and was beloved by all who knew her. The deceased was a daughter of H. Brooke Gwathm
2 CONC ey and Francis Fielding Lewis and her early life was spent in Mobile, Norfolk and Richmond. Her grandfather was Howell Lewis, son of Francia Fielding Lewis and her grandmother was Betty Washington, only sister of George Washington
2 CONC  and with her sister, Mrs. Andrew Reid, of Baltimore, the nearest kin of the father of the country. In 1803 she was married to Adam Empie, regarded at that time as the leading member of the Wilmington bar. Mrs. Empie is survived b
2 CONC y four sons and one daughter, Swift M.( Brooke G., Theodore G., and Adam Empie, this city, and Mrs. Frederick C. Poisson, of London. Two the British army, and Lieutenant Empie Latimer, of the American army, also survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greensboro Daily News
2 CONT Greensboro, North Carolina
2 CONT 20 Jun 1918, Thu • Page 6
