1 NAME Lewis William /Washington/ CSA
2 GIVN Lewis William
2 SURN Washington
2 NSFX CSA
2 _MARNM Washington
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Zion Episcopal Churchyard, Charles Town, Jefferson County, West Virginia, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 NOV 1812
2 PLAC Georgetown, Washington DC
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 OCT 1871
2 PLAC Beall-Air, Jefferson County, Virginia
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 TITL Maj.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -------------------- http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis_Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis William Washington was a great-grandnephew of President George Washington, who is principally remembered as a hostage of abolitionist John Brown's raid on Harpers Ferry, Virginia and as a prosecution witness in the subsequen
2 CONC t trial of Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis Washington was the son of George Corbin Washington, the grandson of William Augustine Washington, and a great-grandson of Augustine Washington, half-brother of George Washington.  Lewis Washington inherited Beall-Air near Ha
2 CONC lltown, West Virginia through his mother, Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas Beall. He made his home at Beal-Air from 1840 until his death in 1871.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Harpers Ferry Raid
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis William Washington inherited several relics of George Washington, including a sword allegedly given by Frederick the Great to Washington and a pair of pistols given by Lafayette. John Cook, who served as John Brown's advance
2 CONC  party at Harpers Ferry, befriended Washington and noted the relics, as well as the slave population at Beall-Air. Brown was fascinated with the Washington relics. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During Brown's October 16, 1859 raid on Harpers Ferry, a detachment from his force led by Cook seized the sword and pistols along with Washington at Beall-Air, taking along three of Washington's slaves. The hostages were taken to 
2 CONC Harpers Ferry by way of the Allstadt House and Ordinary, where more hostages were taken. Ultimately, Washington and the others were held at Brown's base in the fire engine house of the Harpers Ferry federal arsenal. All survived t
2 CONC heir captivity, and Washington identified Brown to the Marine rescue party. During the assault on John Brown's Fort, a saber thrust by Marine Lieutenant Green at Brown was allegedly deflected by the belt buckle securing the Washin
2 CONC gton sword.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many pieces from Lewis Washington's collection of Washington family items, including the sword given him by Frederick the Great and the Lafayette pistols, were donated to the New York State Library by his widow in 1872.
2 CONT
2 CONT During John Brown's trial for treason against the Commonwealth of Virginia, Lewis Washington testified as a witness for the prosecution. During cross-examination, Washington testified that Brown treated his hostages well and gave 
2 CONC orders not to harm civilians.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Civil War began, Washington sided with the Confederacy. On July 17, 1865, he was pardoned by President Andrew Johnson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis Washington married twice, first to Mary Ann Barroll and then to Ella Bassett. He was survived by two sons and two daughters, James Barroll Washington, who served in the Confederate army, Mary Ann Washington (married to Henry
2 CONC  Irving Keyser), Eliza Ridgeley Washington (married Elias Glenn Perine), and William De Hertbrun Washington. William De Hertbrun Washington died without issue on August 30, 1914. James Barroll Washington was survived by one son, W
2 CONC illiam Lanier Washington who died without surviving children on September 11, 1933 after selling the remainder of his family collection of Washington heirlooms at public auction on April 19, 1917.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lewis William Washington and Mary Ann Barroll:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.George Corbin Washington (1837-1843)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.James Barroll Washington (1839-1899)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Mary Ann Washington (1841-1931)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Eliza Ridgeley Washington (1844-1919)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lewis William Washington and Ella Bassett:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Betty Lewis Washington (1861-1862)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.William De Hertbrun Washington (1863-1914)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=78560616
2 CONT
