1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Per Glenn's "The Washingtons: A Family History" volume 1: Seven Generations.... - Noblet, Jr. was raised as an orphan by his aunt, Jane Charlotte Blackburn Washington. He was taken in in 1843 by his cousin, John Au
2 CONC gustine Washington. He went to California in the 'gold rush' of 1849. Benjamin Franklin Washington was the elected leader of this journey. In 1852, he attempted to start a pack train company with three other men. Of these men, two
2 CONC  were inactive partners while the third had temporarily returned to Virginia. Early Fall 1852, he was with 2 hired Mexican hands. Two of his friends searched the area near his camp, including dragging a river. His body was never f
2 CONC ound.
