1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Charles Augustine Thornton''' (1813–1886) is a figure from the American South primarily noted in genealogical and local history circles rather than mainstream historical literature. He belonged to a prominent l
2 CONC anded family with historical roots in Virginia, Mississippi, and Louisiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT ***'''Louisiana Aristocrat'''
2 CONT ***Key Context & Associations:
2 CONT ****Lineage: He married Cornelia Virginia Randolph in 1839, linking him to the historically prominent Randolph family.
2 CONT ****Historical Records: Genealogical platforms highlight his role as a patriarch of the Southern Thornton and Randolph descents.
2 CONT ****Life in the South: He spent his life managing plantations in Louisiana and is buried at the Old Rapides Cemetery in Pineville, Louisiana.
2 CONT ----
