3 CITY Macon
3 STAE MO
3 POST 63552
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Homemaker / Housewife
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Ann Guthrie was the daughter of Benjamin and Nancy (Moore) Young.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Allen Washington Guthrie, the youngest son of Rev. Robert and Mary (Smith) Guthrie, on 16 Sep 1838 in Callaway County, Missouri. Allen was ordained as a minister of the gospel of the Cumberland Presbyterian Church in 1
2 CONC 838. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth gave birth to 10 children. Only the names of 5 are known, and only 4 of them lived to adulthood: Benjamin Eli (1839-1918), Robert James (1843-1883), Virginia A (1846-1877), Barnet M (1849-1849), and Elizabeth Luvenia (18
2 CONC 51-1937)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that Elizabeth Luvenia (Guthrie) Fox's death certificate incorrectly lists her mother's maiden name as Moore rather than Young. Moore was her maternal grandmother's maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
