2 CONT * From Des Cognets, Anna Russell, ''William Russell and His Descendants''. Printed for the Family by Samuel F. Wilson, Lexington, KY., December 1884, page 94 (and available online at https://books.google.com/books?id=rMROAAAAMAAJ&
2 CONC pg=PA123&dq=Gen.+William+Russell&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwib5PzOp8_oAhULbc0KHeBZAJEQ6AEwAHoECAIQAg#v=onepage&q=Grissim&f=false): C. Marry Anne H. Stone, born September 21st 1805, died August 31st 1872....She m
2 CONC arried Capt. Charles Chilton Moore, of Fayette county, Ky., September 5th, 1821, He was born December 1st, 1789, and died August 8d, 1860. Their home, 'Forest Retreat,' was the seat of a generous and widespread hospitality. Their 
2 CONC children were..."b. Hannah  A.R. Moore, married Dr. John D. Grissim, Tennessee. They lived in Fayette county, Ky., whence they removed to Georgetown, Ky., where Dr. Grissim died and Mrs. Grissim now resides."
2 CONT
