2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT B.H. Demint was pastor from 1907-1909. He was quite popular and well respected among the congregation. He later served as president of New Orleans Baptist Theological Seminary.     The Smith Chilton Family, ca. 1910. Front row L t
2 CONC o R with wives standing behind them are the sons of Henry Smith Chilton and Susan (Ransdell) Chilton: John C. Chilton and wife Annie (Wickersham), Henry S. Jr., William Preston and wife Jennie (Chilton), mother, Susan (Ransdell), 
2 CONC George T. and wife Joannie (Sams), James F., Alvin O. and wife Belle (Sams). Henry Smith Chilton was Captain of  I. 4th Regiment Cavalry, Kentucky Volunteers, CSA. Photo courtesy Paul G. Chilton, Campbellsburg and the Henry County
2 CONC  Historical Society.
