1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Is this a relative of the profile above? Same name, same county.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abell-Ransdell Cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Ransdell married Sally Higgins in Mercer County, Kentucky on 20 January 1820; they came to Pettis County in the early 1830s and entered land, including this cemetery. Another pioneer family from Kentucky, George May, also
2 CONC  entered land nearby. The early burials were those of these families and other families related through marriage: Mosby, McFatridge, Mackay, and Bryant. The name Abell was given to the cemetery plot because a Dr. Abell owned the s
2 CONC urrounding farm land for a period of years. There were no burials from this family. The cemetery is kept in good condition, in later years much of this care has been by descendants of the William and Nancy (Cathey) Bryant family. 
2 CONC This cemetery was copied by Mrs. D. M. Middleton and Mrs. Ira A. Leiter, 1 March 1956. Also known as Abell Cemetery An additional transcription appeared in the Prairie Gleaner 2, no. 3 (June 1971), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ransdell Abel Cemetery Flat Creek Township, Pettis County, Missouri Contributed by Laura Paxton, May 2000 [llpaxton@murlin.com]. Total records = 4
