1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On June 4, 1846, she married John Vaughn Smith.
2 CONT Source: Record of the Descendants of John and Elizabeth Bull by James Henry Bull.
2 CONT On December 14, 1872, she married Peter Wainwright Jr. at the Church of the Advent at Boston, Massachusetts. According to her obituary, he was a banker in Philadelphia and the nephew of Bishop Wainwright.
2 CONT Source of marriage: Daily Milwaukee News, Wednesday, January 3, 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Genealogical History of the Ancestors and Descendants of General Robert Bogardus
2 CONT Virginia Adela Parker, the youngest daughter of Commodore Foxhall A. Parker Sr. and Sara Jay Bogardus, was born in New York City about the year 1824. She married for her first husband Dr. Vaughn Smith of the United States Navy. Th
2 CONC ey had one son, Foxhall Parker Smith; he was born at his father's residence at Charlestown, in the Boston Navy Yard, in 1847. He died of typhus fever about 1863, while a midshipman at the Naval Academy in Newport, Rhode Island. He
2 CONC  was a young man of great promise.
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia Adela Parker married, for her second husband, Peter Wainwright, a nephew of Bishop Wainwright. They had no children. Her death occurred at Washington, D.C. on August 1, 1904 and her remains are interred in the family plot
2 CONC  in Ronaldson Cemetery at Philadelphia.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/183299962/virginia_adela_wainwright Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 10 2024, 6:06:3
2 CONC 7 UTC''
