1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=27185081
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Richmond only son of Reverend William Fitzhugh Lee and Mary Catharine Simms Chilton, his father was a brother of Edmund Jennings Lee, Sr.. He married Lily Parran on September 15, 1850, daughter of Dr. Richard and Laura Par
2 CONC ran of Shepherdstown, Jefferson County, Virginia. In 1853 he graduated from the Virginia Military Institute in Lexington, Virginia. On August 1, 1853 he received commission as 2nd Lieutenant of the 2nd US Infantry from secretary o
2 CONC f war Jefferson Davis. He served with Captain J.E.B. Stuart at Fort Leavenworth. Resigning his commission on April 30, 1861 with the secession of Virginia he gave his services to the Confederate States Army, Captain of the 33rd Vi
2 CONC rginia Infantry. Mortally wounded on July 21, 1861 at First Manassas while acting as Field Lieutenant Colonel.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 33rd Virginia Infantry  Regiment, Stonewall Brigade, Army Of Northern Virginia, CSA. Killed at the battle of First Manassas. This memorial was created by Bill Jordan.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/27185081/willi
2 CONC am-fitzhugh-lee Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 6 2019, 3:19:09 UTC''
