1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/6161675/john-hicks-george
2 CONT
2 CONT George joined William Clark Quantrills Army in 1862. Union soldiers hung him until he was almost dead, in hopes he would confess about Quantrill's involvement in the Lawrence, Kansas raid on August 21, 1863. John also joined Gener
2 CONC al Joseph Orville Shelby's brigade, and was captured at Ft. Scott, Kansas in 1864 and sent to Federal's prison at Rock Island Illinois. He was exchanged at Richmond and then went to North and South Carolina. He surrendered at Shre
2 CONC veport, Louisiana, May 1865. Father was David George.
2 CONT
