1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1st wife, Jane died, maternal parents tried to steal the grandchildren from JQA, so he moved with his mother and the children to Fannin Co. Texas, Fannin Co., Texas, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Rogers (Arkansas) Democrat, 15 February 1917, from The Madison County (Arkansas) Democrat John Quincy Adams Warren, age about 90 years, was going from Drake’s Creek to his home near Roxton Tuesday afternoon when his clothing caugh
2 CONC t fire from matches in his pocket that are supposed to have been ignited by fire from his pipe, which he had placed in his pocket among the matches and he was so severely burned that death resulted the following morning about 7 o’
2 CONC clock. The old man was alone, driving an ox team, as had been his custom ever since he had resided in this county, and was near the farm house of P. S. (Pleasant) Scott when he discovered his clothing was on fire. He wore a heavy 
2 CONC overcoat in addition to his other apparel and had about succeeded in removing all of his garments when parties who heard his cries for help reached him but his injuries were fatal and the medical aid which was promptly rendered to
2 CONC  him could only serve to alleviate his suffering. The deceased was a U. S. soldier in the war between this government and Mexico in 1845-48, also served as a federal soldier in the Civil war and later rendered valuable service to 
2 CONC the United States during the Indian wars of the 70’s. He drew a liberal pension for the government, sufficient for the support of himself and wife, who survives him, but he was not content to be idle and each year cultivated a cro
2 CONC p on his farm, using his oxen in preference to horses or mules in drawing his modern riding plows and cultivators. His last trip to Huntsville was made last week in a light spring hack to which was hitched his young yoke of oxen, 
2 CONC a well matched pair of Jerseys, in which he took great pride. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
