1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Profile photo from: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reno_Gang
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Franklin Reno (Frank): '''Crime Figure. One of the outlaw Reno brothers, hanged by vigilantes in the New Albany, Indiana jail. Famous for the first train robbery, just outside Seymour, Indiana on October 6, 1866. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Reno Gang was a group of criminals that operated in the Midwestern United States during and just after the American Civil War. Though short-lived, they carried out the first three peacetime train robberies in U.S. history. Mos
2 CONC t of the stolen money was never recovered. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reno_Gang
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source: '''
