2 CONT
2 CONT Simeon Reno was a member of the Reno Gang,  a group of criminals that operated in the Midwestern United States during and just after the American Civil War. Though short-lived, they carried out the first three peacetime train robb
2 CONC eries in U.S. history. Most of the stolen money was never recovered. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reno_Gang
2 CONT
2 CONT Simeon Reno, b. August 02, 1843, Jackson Co., IN; d. December 12, 1868, hanged in New Albany, Indiana jail by vigilantes; buried Seymour cemetery. His parents were: Wilkison Reno and Julia Ann Freyhafer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He defrauded the government of enlistment and bounty money by falsely enlisting twice, which enabled him to obtain bounty money from the county as well. He enrolled March 22, 1865 in the 79th Regiment at Columbus, IN, but was must
2 CONC ered out at Indianapolis on May 19, 1865. On March 28, 1865, he again enrolled as a private in Company H, 13th Regiment, and was mustered the same day at Columbus, IN. His record indicates that he deserted on May 12, 1865.* Refere
2 CONC nce: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18719/simeon-reno Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 17 2021, 21:57:15 UTC''
