1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8224017/strother-moses-hawkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Strother M. Hawkins, Jr. was the son of Strother M. Hawkins, Sr. and Francis Lucinda Reno. His brothers and sisters were: Mary Frances Hawkins, James Wm. Hawkins, Hulda Elizabeth Hawkins, Joseph S. Hawkins, Elizabeth Jane Hawkins 
2 CONC and Samuel Hawkins. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Obit from Greeneville Tex. Evenine Banner, Tuesday August 24, 1920, Page 1: "Stroud Hawkind: Died at Ivanhoe Monday Stroud Hawkins, former Greevnille man, and for many years a resident of Hunt County, died yesterday at Ivanhoe, ac
2 CONC cording to information received here this monring. It was stated that the remains will be brought to Greenville today and that funeral services will be held tomorrow, although there were no final arrangements made for the funeral 
2 CONC penidng the arrival of the body. The remains of Mr. Hawkins will arrive in this city this afternoon and the funeral will take place tomorrow morning at 10:0Clock; burial in East Mount Cemetery."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
