2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Harrodsburg bred Leonatus, winner of the ninth Kentucky Derby (1883), was owned by https://www.geni.com/people/George-Morgan/6000000225197498887 and Colonel Jack P. Chinn, both of Mercer County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chinn also co-bred 1916 Kentucky Derby winner George Smith, who won his first seven races and 11 stakes over his career and was the famous namesake of the professional gambler better known as Pittsburg Phil. 
