1 CONT David McCarty heirs deed, 1800, Shenandoah Co., Virginia Court Records
1 CONT _________________
1 CONT
1 CONT Let this Instrument testify that John McCartey of the County of Shenandoah, John Hurst of the same county and Mary his wife, Absolom Hurst of the County and Catharina his wife, Jessee Hurst of the County of [blank] and Nancy his w
1 CONC ife. Sally McCartey, Betsy McCarty, Thomas McCarty and William McCartey all of the said County of Shendoah [sic] (which said John, Sally, Betsey, Thomas and William McCarty, Mary, Catherina and Nancy Hurst are children & heirs of 
1 CONC David McCarty deceased) for the consideration of fifty pounds to them paid in equal portions by John Gray of the County of Caroline the receipt of which is hereby acknowledged have granted bargained and sold and do hereby grant ba
1 CONC rgain and sell unto the said John Gray all that tract or parcel of Land being in Caroline County containing by estimation fifty eight acres be the same, more or less which was purchased by the said David McCarty deceased of Reuben
1 CONC  Mondag and Sarah his wife and conveyed by deed recorded in the Court of the sd. County of Caroline with all its pertaining rights, proffits & priviledges. To hold the said tract of land and premises unto the said John Gray his he
1 CONC irs & assigns to his and their own use, free from and indemnified against the claim right and title of the Vendors, and each of them, their heirs, and all others whatsoever. In Witness whereof the said Vendors have hereunto set th
1 CONC eir hands and Seals this first day of January one thousand eight hundred.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sealed and delivered John McCarty (Seal)
1 CONT in presence of us John Hurst (Seal)
1 CONT Jno. Dajarnald [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT Georg Hopkins [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT Jos. Loughlin [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT Theophilus Fovier [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT Sally McCarty (her x mark) Seal)
1 CONT [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT [blank] (Seal)
1 CONT
1 CONT At a Court held for Shenandoah County on Monday Sept. the 8th 1800
1 CONT
1 CONT This Indenture of Bargain and Sale from John McCarty, John Hurst & Mary his wife Absolom Hurst and Catharina his wife Jesse Hurst and Nancy his wife Sally McCarty Betsy McCarty Thomas McCarty and William McCarty to John Gray was a
1 CONC cknowledged by John McCarty and Elizabeth his wife she being first privily examined as the Law directs, and Sally McCarty and ordered to be recorded as to them...
1 CONT
1 CONT Teste
1 CONT Ph. Williams
