0 @N6000000002906180244@ NOTE Will of Ann Nancy Conway Oldham Aughey, mother of Nancy Ann Oldham Rector, mentions granddaughter Nancy Rector.   Transcript of attested copy in the collection of the Filson Club, Louisville, KY 4 March 1936:  "IN THE NAME OF GOD,
1 CONC  AMEN, I Anna Aughey, of the County of Hampshire and State of Virginia considering the uncertainty of this mortal life and being of sound and perfect mind and memory, blessed by Almighty God for the same, do make and publish this 
1 CONC my last will and testament in manner and form following, that is to say:
1 CONT      First, I give and bequeath to my grand-son, Samuel Bray, the following slaves by name Peg, a woman, Peter, a boy, Rachel, a girl, and Mary, a girl and also I give and bequeath unto my beloved son, Saml. Oldham, the sum of one
1 CONC  shilling sterling, Also I give and bequeath to my daughter, Wineford Nevil the sum of one shilling sterling.  Also I give and bequeath to my daughter Abigil Lyal one shilling, Also I give and bequeath to my daughter, Susannah Ros
1 CONC s, one shilling.  Also I give and bequeath to my daughter, Mary Ann Kirkpatrick the sum of one shilling and also I give and bequeath to my daughter, Nancy Rector the sum of one shilling and lastly as to all the rest, residue, and 
1 CONC remainder of my house-hold and kitchen furniture and of my personal estate, goods, and chattels of what kind or nature soever that I may possess at my decease, it is my will that they be equally divided acording to quallety and qu
1 CONC antity between my two grand-children, Samual Bray and Nancy Rector, and also I do hereby appoint Conway Rector and Samuel Bray, sole Executors of this my last will and testament, hereby revoking all former wills by me made.  In wi
1 CONC tness whereof, I have hereunto set my hand and seal the seventeenth day of November in the year of our Lord one thousand seven hundred and ninety five.
1 CONT                                                         her
1 CONT                                                     Anna    Aughney (Seal)
1 CONT                                                         mark.
1 CONT Signed, Sealed, Published, and Declared by the above named Anna Aughney to be her last will and testament of us the subscribers.
1 CONT                                         George Currulkers, Daniel McLaughlen,
1 CONT                                         William Young, John Higgins.
1 CONT
1 CONT At a Court held for Hampshire County the 15th day of April, 1796, this last will & testament of Ann Aughney, deceased, was proved by the oaths of William Young and John Higgins two of the witnesses thereto and is ordered to be rec
1 CONC orded.
1 CONT                                         Test.  And. Wodrow, Cl. Cur.
1 CONT
1 CONT A TRUE COPY
1 CONT     Attest:  R.C. Stewart, Clerk
1 CONT              Cty. Ct. Hamp. Co., W.Va.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Will Book No. 1-22, pg. 51."
1 CONT copy of will  provided by Jeanne W. Jackson, 772 Apple Ave., Ukiah, CA 95482
